(55, 1, '2004-2005', 25, 'Enrich TLE‑TVL with Industry Partnerships', '**Enrich TLE‑TVL with Industry Partnerships**\nBuilding on the recent score rise, deepen practical relevance for students.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a bi‑annual industry needs survey and map findings to TLE‑TVL modules (indicator 1.8), reporting by 15 May each year.\n- Grade Level Leaders to co‑design two new TLE‑TVL units per semester incorporating survey results, with lesson plans submitted within two weeks after design meetings.\n- ALS Coordinator to launch a pilot apprenticeship program for senior students, enrolling at least 10 learners per cycle and providing monthly progress reports.', 'Last cycle: “Boost Curriculum Relevance via Industry Partnerships”; Result: score improved by 7.8 from 74.1% to 81.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:33:04', 0),
(56, 1, '2004-2005', 26, 'Expand Inclusive Access and Strengthen DRRM Preparedness', '**Expand Inclusive Access and Strengthen DRRM Preparedness**\nAddress the dip in learning environment score by ensuring all learners can safely participate.\n- Guidance Counselor to hold bi‑monthly community outreach to identify disadvantaged, OSY, and adult learners (indicator 2.5), compiling enrollment lists within five days of each session.\n- Facilities Officer to conduct quarterly checks of classroom accessibility and DRRM equipment, updating a compliance log by the 10th of the following month.\n- ALS Coordinator to develop a term‑based DRRM awareness workshop for all learners, delivering it at least once per term and submitting attendance records within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Expand Inclusive Access for Disadvantaged Learners”; Result: score declined by 9.0 from 80.5% to 71.5%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 71.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:33:04', 0),
(57, 1, '2004-2005', 27, 'Cultivate Distributed Leadership and Mentorship', '**Cultivate Distributed Leadership and Mentorship**\nLeverage the strong leadership score to embed mentorship across school functions.\n- Assistant Principal to match each emerging leader with a senior mentor, scheduling bi‑monthly meetings and recording action points within one week (indicator 3.2).\n- School Head to organize quarterly leadership reflection workshops with the School‑Community Planning Team, producing concise minutes and next‑step lists.\n- Community Liaison Officer to coordinate an annual community‑leadership forum, inviting local partners and reporting outcomes to the division by 15 May.', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Emerging Leaders through Structured Mentoring”; Result: score declined by 3.1 from 88.1% to 85.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:33:04', 0),
(58, 1, '2004-2005', 28, 'Strengthen Stakeholder Collaboration Framework', '**Strengthen Stakeholder Collaboration Framework**\nEnhance partnership quality to boost governance performance.\n- Governance Committee Chair to adopt a standardized meeting agenda and minutes template for monthly SGC sessions (indicator 4.2), circulating minutes within three days.\n- Strategic Planning Officer to conduct a semi‑annual audit of council decisions and partnership outcomes, presenting findings to the school board by the 20th of the audit month.\n- School Secretary to update the public KPI dashboard quarterly, adding a governance partnerships widget and notifying stakeholders via email (indicator 4.4).', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Governance Council Effectiveness”; Result: score was unchanged from 79.2% to 79.2%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:33:04', 0),
(59, 1, '2004-2005', 29, 'Systematize Staff Performance and Development', '**Systematize Staff Performance and Development**\nBuild on the modest improvement to ensure consistent staff growth.\n- HR Officer to implement a monthly performance commitment checklist for all staff (indicator 5.2), completing reviews by the 5th of each month.\n- Department Heads to hold quarterly staff appraisal meetings, recording scores and development plans within one week.\n- Principal to recognize top performers in a bi‑annual ceremony aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and publish highlights on the school intranet.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate Office Performance Commitment”; Result: score improved by 3.5 from 76.1% to 79.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:33:04', 0),
(60, 1, '2004-2005', 30, 'Optimize MOOE Utilization and Financial Monitoring', '**Optimize MOOE Utilization and Financial Monitoring**\nTarget the low utilization rating to improve resource efficiency.\n- Finance Officer to produce a quarterly variance analysis of MOOE expenditures (indicator 6.6) and present findings to the principal by the 10th of the following month.\n- Facilities Manager to update the five‑year infrastructure roadmap annually, prioritizing safety‑critical projects and submitting the revised draft to the school council by 30 April.\n- Principal to authorize a bi‑annual internal audit of procurement processes, delivering a compliance report with recommendations within 30 days of each audit.', 'Last cycle: “Refine Financial Monitoring and Infrastructure Planning”; Result: score declined by 9.3 from 87.9% to 78.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 78.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:33:04', 0),
(61, 1, '2004-2005', 25, 'Refresh curriculum alignment and instructional design', 'Leverage the recent score gain to deepen curriculum relevance and instructional quality. Implement systematic reviews and collaborative planning.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a quarterly curriculum audit ensuring alignment with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and submit findings within two weeks after each audit.\n- Grade Level Leaders to design and integrate cross‑subject project‑based learning units, delivering lesson plans monthly for peer review.\n- Assessment Team to analyze term‑end student performance data and present actionable insights to teachers within ten days of results release.', 'Last cycle: “Boost Curriculum Relevance via Industry Partnerships”; Result: score improved by 7.8 from 74.1% to 81.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:42:03', 0);
INSERT INTO `ai_suggestion_history` (`id`, `school_id`, `school_year`, `dimension_id`, `suggestion_title`, `suggestion_text`, `last_cycle_note`, `priority_label`, `decline_risk`, `data_status`, `score_at_time`, `model_version`, `is_final`, `needs_review`, `adopted_plan_id`, `generated_by`, `generated_at`, `is_sample`) VALUES
(62, 1, '2004-2005', 26, 'Strengthen learning environment accessibility and safety', 'Address the notable dip by improving safety planning and expanding access for disadvantaged learners. Target concrete, measurable actions.\n- Facilities Officer to review and update the school\'s DRRM plan, completing revisions by end of Q2 (indicator 2.8) and circulate to staff.\n- Guidance Counselor to identify disadvantaged, OSY, and adult learners, compiling an enrollment list each month and ensuring enrollment within five days (indicator 2.5).\n- School Head to conduct monthly classroom accessibility walkthroughs, documenting barrier‑free status and reporting compliance within three days of each check.', 'Last cycle: “Expand Inclusive Access for Disadvantaged Learners”; Result: score declined by 9.0 from 80.5% to 71.5%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 71.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 182, 37, '2026-10-11 17:42:03', 0),
(63, 1, '2004-2005', 27, 'Deepen leadership capacity and peer mentorship', 'Even with a solid score, the decline signals a need for sustained leadership development. Focus on structured mentorship and reflective practice.\n- Assistant Principal to launch a quarterly leadership development forum, rotating themes and documenting action items within one week.\n- School Head to implement a semi‑annual peer‑review of leadership practices, producing a concise report and improvement checklist for each leader.\n- Community Liaison Officer to coordinate a bi‑monthly mentorship pairing between senior administrators and emerging leaders, recording meeting minutes and next steps.', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Emerging Leaders through Structured Mentoring”; Result: score declined by 3.1 from 88.1% to 85.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:42:03', 0),
(64, 1, '2004-2005', 28, 'Expand stakeholder partnerships and governance rigor', 'Enhance collaboration to boost governance outcomes, especially given the unchanged score. Prioritize partnership actions.\n- Governance Committee Chair to convene bi‑monthly stakeholder partnership meetings, recording agreements and following up on actions (indicator 4.4).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to draft a quarterly partnership action plan, presenting progress to the school council each quarter.\n- School Secretary to update the public KPI dashboard with a dedicated partnership metrics widget, publishing updates monthly and notifying stakeholders via email.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Governance Council Effectiveness”; Result: score was unchanged from 79.2% to 79.2%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 183, 37, '2026-10-11 17:42:03', 0),
(65, 1, '2004-2005', 29, 'Elevate staff development and recognition', 'Build on the modest score rise by institutionalizing continuous professional growth and visible acknowledgment of excellence.\n- HR Officer to launch a quarterly professional development needs survey, compiling results and action plans within two weeks of each survey.\n- Department Heads to hold monthly staff coaching circles, documenting key takeaways and follow‑up tasks.\n- Principal to conduct a bi‑annual awards ceremony recognizing top performers, aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and publish highlights on the school intranet.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate Office Performance Commitment”; Result: score improved by 3.5 from 76.1% to 79.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:42:03', 0),
(66, 1, '2004-2005', 30, 'Optimize MOOE utilization and financial oversight', 'Counter the sharp decline by tightening monitoring of operating expenses and reinforcing fiscal accountability.\n- Finance Officer to track monthly MOOE utilization, aiming for at least 85% usage, and submit a utilization report by the 5th of the following month (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to prepare a quarterly maintenance priority list aligned with the MOOE budget, delivering it to the Finance Officer before the end of each quarter.\n- Principal to organize an annual financial stewardship workshop for school managers, scheduled each June, with post‑workshop action plans submitted within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Refine Financial Monitoring and Infrastructure Planning”; Result: score declined by 9.3 from 87.9% to 78.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 78.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:42:03', 0),
(67, 1, '2004-2005', 25, 'Enhance curriculum relevance and instructional quality', 'Align learning outcomes with industry standards and strengthen teacher capacity.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a curriculum audit against DepEd standards and produce a gap report by 30 April (quarterly review).\n- Grade Level Leaders to organize monthly professional development workshops on differentiated instruction and technology integration, documenting attendance and outcomes.\n- School Head to pilot two interdisciplinary project‑based learning units per semester, with lesson plans submitted within two weeks after design and evaluated through student performance data.', 'Last cycle: “Boost Curriculum Relevance via Industry Partnerships”; Result: score improved by 7.8 from 74.1% to 81.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:50:24', 0),
(68, 1, '2004-2005', 26, 'Expand inclusive learning access and strengthen safety planning', 'Improve facilities and outreach for disadvantaged learners while ensuring disaster readiness.\n- Guidance Counselor to conduct bi‑monthly community outreach to identify eligible out‑of‑school youth, compiling enrollment lists within five days (indicator 2.5).\n- Facilities Officer to perform monthly barrier‑free classroom inspections and remediate identified obstacles within ten days.\n- Safety Officer to review and update the school DRRM plan quarterly, conducting a drill each term and submitting a compliance report within seven days after each drill (indicator 2.8).', 'Last cycle: “Expand Inclusive Access for Disadvantaged Learners”; Result: score declined by 9.0 from 80.5% to 71.5%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 71.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:50:24', 0),
(69, 1, '2004-2005', 27, 'Deepen leadership development and collaborative planning', 'Build a culture of shared leadership and continuous improvement.\n- Assistant Principal to establish a peer‑coaching circle for emerging leaders, meeting bi‑monthly and recording action items within three days.\n- School Head to convene a quarterly School‑Community Planning Team workshop focused on data‑driven decision‑making, producing concise minutes and next‑step lists.\n- Community Liaison Officer to organize an annual community‑leadership forum by 15 May, inviting local partners and summarizing outcomes for the division.', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Emerging Leaders through Structured Mentoring”; Result: score declined by 3.1 from 88.1% to 85.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:50:24', 0),
(70, 1, '2004-2005', 28, 'Strengthen governance collaboration and transparency', 'Enhance stakeholder partnerships and accountability mechanisms.\n- Governance Committee Chair to adopt a standardized meeting agenda and minutes template for all monthly SGC sessions, circulating minutes within three days (indicator 4.4).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to host a semi‑annual partnership forum with neighboring schools and NGOs, documenting joint initiatives and reporting outcomes to the school board by the 20th of the forum month.\n- School Secretary to refresh the public KPI dashboard quarterly, adding a stakeholder‑engagement widget and notifying stakeholders via email.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Governance Council Effectiveness”; Result: score was unchanged from 79.2% to 79.2%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:50:24', 0),
(71, 1, '2004-2005', 29, 'Advance staff performance management and recognition', 'Consolidate gains in staff appraisal and celebrate excellence.\n- HR Officer to implement a monthly performance commitment checklist for all staff, completing reviews by the 5th of each month.\n- Department Heads to hold quarterly staff appraisal meetings, recording scores and development plans within one week.\n- Principal to organize a bi‑annual awards ceremony aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, publishing highlights on the school intranet within two weeks after the event.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate Office Performance Commitment”; Result: score improved by 3.5 from 76.1% to 79.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:50:24', 0),
(72, 1, '2004-2005', 30, 'Optimize MOOE utilization and financial oversight', 'Ensure efficient use of operating expenses and strengthen monitoring.\n- Finance Officer to produce a quarterly variance analysis of MOOE expenditures, presenting findings to the principal by the 10th of the following month (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to update the five‑year infrastructure roadmap annually, prioritizing safety‑critical projects and submitting the revised draft to the school council by 30 April.\n- Principal to commission a bi‑annual internal audit of procurement processes, delivering a compliance report with recommendations within 30 days of each audit.', 'Last cycle: “Refine Financial Monitoring and Infrastructure Planning”; Result: score declined by 9.3 from 87.9% to 78.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 78.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 17:50:24', 0),
(73, 1, '2005-2006', 25, 'Refresh Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Practices', '**Curriculum and Teaching**\nThe recent dip signals a need to revisit curriculum coherence and teacher support.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to develop a competency‑based curriculum map aligned with DepEd K‑12 standards and share it school‑wide by 15 May.\n- Grade Level Leaders to implement a peer‑observation cycle where teachers observe each other twice per term and provide structured feedback within five days.\n- School Head to introduce a quarterly data‑review meeting using student assessment results to adjust instructional strategies, with action plans documented within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum relevance and instructional quality”; Result: score declined by 7.2 from 81.9% to 74.7%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 74.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:14:09', 0),
(74, 1, '2005-2006', 26, 'Strengthen Safe and Inclusive Learning Environment', '**Learning Environment**\nA slight decline highlights the need to reinforce safety and inclusion measures.\n- Safety Officer to launch a school‑wide anti‑bullying campaign with monthly assemblies and a reporting system, reviewing incidents weekly (indicator 2.1).\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to conduct quarterly training for staff on safeguarding protocols and submit a compliance report within seven days (indicator 2.7).\n- Guidance Counselor to establish a mentorship program for at‑risk students, meeting bi‑monthly and tracking attendance.', 'Last cycle: “Expand inclusive learning access and strengthen safety planning”; Result: score declined by 0.2 from 71.5% to 71.3%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 71.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 185, 37, '2026-10-11 18:14:09', 0),
(75, 1, '2005-2006', 27, 'Cultivate Shared Leadership and Data‑Driven Planning', '**Leadership**\nThe ten‑point drop calls for stronger collaborative governance.\n- Assistant Principal to design a leadership development roadmap with quarterly milestones, reviewed by the principal each quarter.\n- School Head to institute a rotating chair system for the School‑Community Planning Team, changing chair every term and documenting decisions within three days (indicator 3.2).\n- Community Liaison Officer to create a stakeholder feedback survey after each major school event, analyzing results within two weeks and sharing with the leadership team.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen leadership development and collaborative planning”; Result: score declined by 10.0 from 85.0% to 75.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Medium', 'low', 'sufficient', 75.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 186, 37, '2026-10-11 18:14:09', 0),
(76, 1, '2005-2006', 28, 'Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Engagement', '**Governance and Accountability**\nThe decline suggests a need for clearer processes and stakeholder feedback.\n- Governance Committee Chair to launch an online procurement transparency portal, updating entries weekly and notifying the council.\n- Strategic Planning Officer to conduct an annual stakeholder satisfaction survey, compiling results and presenting recommendations by 31 July (indicator 4.6).\n- School Secretary to maintain a searchable archive of all SGC meeting minutes, uploading them within two days of each meeting (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen governance collaboration and transparency”; Result: score declined by 8.4 from 79.2% to 70.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 70.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 189, 37, '2026-10-11 18:14:09', 0),
(77, 1, '2005-2006', 29, 'Boost Staff Performance Management and Recognition', '**Human Resource and Team Development**\nThe score drop indicates room to improve appraisal consistency and morale.\n- HR Officer to create individualized Professional Growth Plans for all staff, reviewed semi‑annually and updated by 15 June (indicator 5.2).\n- Department Heads to launch a peer‑recognition board highlighting exemplary practices monthly, with entries submitted by staff within five days.\n- Principal to set up a mentorship program pairing experienced teachers with newcomers, meeting monthly and reporting progress to the HR office (indicator 5.5).', 'Last cycle: “Advance staff performance management and recognition”; Result: score declined by 7.5 from 79.6% to 72.1%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 72.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 190, 37, '2026-10-11 18:14:09', 0),
(78, 1, '2005-2006', 30, 'Optimize Financial Management and Facility Oversight', '**Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization**\nThe notable decline calls for tighter expense monitoring and infrastructure planning.\n- Finance Officer to implement an electronic expense approval system, ensuring all MOOE requests are logged and approved within three business days (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to conduct monthly facility condition surveys and update the infrastructure maintenance schedule, submitting a summary report by the 10th of each month (indicator 6.1).\n- Principal to form a Cost‑Saving Task Force comprising teachers and staff, meeting bi‑monthly to identify savings opportunities and report recommendations within five days.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize MOOE utilization and financial oversight”; Result: score declined by 8.6 from 78.6% to 70.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Medium', 'low', 'sufficient', 70.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 191, 37, '2026-10-11 18:14:09', 0),
(79, 1, '2006-2007', 25, 'Enhance curriculum alignment and instructional support', 'Align the curriculum more closely with DepEd K‑12 standards and strengthen teacher collaboration.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a gap analysis of the current syllabus versus DepEd K‑12 standards by 30 April and share findings with teachers.\n- Grade Level Leaders to schedule monthly collaborative lesson‑planning workshops focusing on competency‑based outcomes, uploading minutes within two days.\n- School Head to institute a bi‑monthly review of student performance data, linking trends to curriculum adjustments and documenting a brief report within five days of each review.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Practices”; Result: score change unavailable, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 76.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:41:17', 0),
(80, 1, '2006-2007', 26, 'Strengthen inclusive and safe learning spaces', 'Build on existing safety measures while expanding access for disadvantaged learners.\n- Safety Officer to maintain monthly anti‑bullying assemblies and conduct quarterly incident audits (indicator 2.1).\n- Guidance Counselor to expand the mentorship program to include at least ten disadvantaged or out‑of‑school youth, meeting bi‑monthly with attendance logged by the 5th of the following month.\n- Learning Resources Coordinator to audit classroom resources and secure additional materials for OSY and adult learners, completing procurement by 15 June in line with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Safe and Inclusive Learning Environment”; Result: score change unavailable, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 75.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:41:17', 0),
(81, 1, '2006-2007', 27, 'Foster innovative leadership for frontline services', 'Encourage leadership practices that generate new service ideas for stakeholders.\n- Assistant Principal to launch a quarterly “Innovation Lab” where staff prototype service improvements, presenting prototypes to the School‑Community Planning Team within two weeks.\n- School Head to recognize one innovative frontline initiative each term through a formal award, documented in the school newsletter.\n- Community Liaison Officer to gather stakeholder feedback on new services via short surveys after each major event, summarizing results within five days (indicator 3.4).', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Shared Leadership and Data‑Driven Planning”; Result: score change unavailable, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 76.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:41:17', 0),
(82, 1, '2006-2007', 28, 'Sustain transparent governance practices', 'Maintain and deepen the transparency gains achieved in recent cycles.\n- Governance Committee Chair to update the online procurement portal weekly and publish a summary of expenditures by the 10th of each month.\n- Strategic Planning Officer to conduct an annual stakeholder satisfaction survey, presenting findings to the SGC by 31 July (indicator 4.6).\n- School Secretary to ensure all SGC meeting minutes are uploaded to the shared drive within two days of each meeting and to create a searchable index by the end of the semester.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Engagement”; Result: score change unavailable, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:41:17', 0),
(83, 1, '2006-2007', 29, 'Advance staff development and recognition', 'Build on existing professional growth initiatives to boost morale and effectiveness.\n- HR Officer to finalize individualized Professional Growth Plans for all teachers by 15 June, reviewing progress semi‑annually (indicator 5.2).\n- Department Heads to rotate a peer‑recognition spotlight in monthly staff meetings, with nominations submitted three days prior.\n- Principal to establish a quarterly mentorship circle pairing veteran teachers with new staff, reporting outcomes to HR within ten days after each session (indicator 5.5).', 'Last cycle: “Boost Staff Performance Management and Recognition”; Result: score change unavailable, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:41:17', 0),
(84, 1, '2006-2007', 30, 'Enhance financial oversight and resource planning', 'Strengthen expense monitoring and infrastructure maintenance to sustain fiscal health.\n- Finance Officer to fully implement the electronic expense approval system for all MOOE requests, ensuring logs are completed within three business days (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to conduct monthly facility condition surveys and update the maintenance schedule, submitting a summary by the 10th of each month (indicator 6.1).\n- Principal to convene a bi‑monthly Cost‑Saving Task Force, tasked with identifying at least two savings opportunities per meeting and reporting recommendations within five days.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize Financial Management and Facility Oversight”; Result: score change unavailable, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:41:17', 0),
(85, 1, '2006-2007', 25, 'Enhance Curriculum Coherence', '**Strengthen curriculum delivery**\nAlign learning outcomes with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024 and ensure consistent implementation.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to finalize a competency‑based curriculum map and share school‑wide by 30 April.\n- Grade Level Leaders to hold monthly collaborative lesson‑planning sessions, documenting adjustments within three days.\n- School Head to convene quarterly data‑review meetings using assessment results, producing action plans within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Practices”; Result: score improved by 2.2 from 74.7% to 76.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 76.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:42:57', 0),
(86, 1, '2006-2007', 26, 'Promote Inclusive and Safe Learning Spaces', '**Foster inclusive and secure environments**\nTarget disadvantaged learners and maintain a zero‑incidence record for child abuse.\n- Guidance Counselor to launch an outreach program for OSYs and adult learners, meeting monthly and reporting enrollment numbers (indicator 2.5).\n- Child Protection Officer to conduct bi‑weekly child‑protection audits and update the zero‑incidence log (indicator 2.2).\n- Facilities Manager to complete accessibility upgrades for classrooms serving disadvantaged students by the end of the term.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Safe and Inclusive Learning Environment”; Result: score improved by 4.2 from 71.3% to 75.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 75.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:42:57', 0),
(87, 1, '2006-2007', 27, 'Drive Innovative Leadership Practices', '**Advance frontline service innovation**\nLeverage technology and community partnerships to improve service delivery.\n- Assistant Principal to pilot a digital feedback platform for parents and students, launch by 15 June and review usage monthly.\n- School Head to organize a quarterly Innovation Showcase where teachers present service improvements, documenting outcomes within five days.\n- Community Liaison Officer to coordinate quarterly projects with local NGOs, reporting results (indicator 3.4).', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Shared Leadership and Data‑Driven Planning”; Result: score improved by 1.3 from 75.0% to 76.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 76.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:42:57', 0),
(88, 1, '2006-2007', 28, 'Strengthen Governance Transparency', '**Enhance governance and accountability**\nBuild on recent gains by increasing openness and systematic monitoring.\n- Governance Committee Chair to publish quarterly financial and procurement summaries on the school website within 10 days of quarter‑end.\n- Strategic Planning Officer to conduct an annual risk assessment and present recommendations to the SGC by 31 August.\n- School Secretary to digitize all meeting minutes and maintain a searchable archive, uploading documents within two days of each meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Engagement”; Result: score improved by 12.5 from 70.8% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:42:57', 0),
(89, 1, '2006-2007', 29, 'Boost Staff Development and Morale', '**Elevate human resource and team development**\nSustain professional growth and recognize exemplary practices.\n- HR Officer to launch a quarterly professional‑development grant program, with applications due 15 of each quarter.\n- Department Heads to implement monthly peer‑observation cycles using structured feedback forms, completed within three days.\n- Principal to hold bi‑monthly staff wellness check‑ins and submit a summary report to HR by the end of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Boost Staff Performance Management and Recognition”; Result: score improved by 7.9 from 72.1% to 80.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:42:57', 0),
(90, 1, '2006-2007', 30, 'Optimize Financial Management', '**Improve finance and resource mobilization**\nLeverage technology and strategic planning for efficient resource use.\n- Finance Officer to integrate an online budgeting dashboard accessible to department heads, updated monthly.\n- Facilities Manager to develop a five‑year infrastructure master plan, draft due 31 March and review semi‑annually.\n- Principal to convene a bi‑annual resource‑mobilization forum with PTAs and local businesses, delivering action‑item reports within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize Financial Management and Facility Oversight”; Result: score improved by 15.0 from 70.0% to 85.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:42:57', 0),
(91, 1, '2006-2007', 25, 'Strengthen curriculum mapping and collaborative planning', '**Curriculum and Teaching**\nTo enhance curriculum coherence and instructional quality, focus on systematic mapping and shared planning.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to develop a competency‑based curriculum map aligned with DepEd K‑12 standards and share school‑wide by 15 May (DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024).\n- Grade Level Leaders to hold monthly collaborative lesson‑planning workshops, documenting shared resources within five days.\n- School Head to convene quarterly data‑review meetings using student assessment results, producing action plans within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Practices”; Result: score improved by 2.2 from 74.7% to 76.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 76.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:43:51', 0),
(92, 1, '2006-2007', 26, 'Enhance safety, inclusion, and access for disadvantaged learners', '**Learning Environment**\nMaintain a safe, inclusive setting while expanding learning opportunities for disadvantaged groups.\n- Safety Officer to continue the anti‑bullying campaign with monthly assemblies and weekly incident reviews (indicator 2.1).\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to conduct quarterly safeguarding training and submit compliance reports within seven days (indicator 2.7).\n- Guidance Counselor to expand the mentorship program to include out‑of‑school youth and adult learners, meeting bi‑monthly and tracking attendance (indicator 2.5).', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Safe and Inclusive Learning Environment”; Result: score improved by 4.2 from 71.3% to 75.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 75.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 192, 37, '2026-10-11 18:43:51', 0),
(93, 1, '2006-2007', 27, 'Boost collaborative leadership and service innovation', '**Leadership**\nStrengthen collaborative governance and encourage innovative frontline services.\n- Assistant Principal to refine the leadership development roadmap with quarterly milestones and add an annual innovation showcase for staff (indicator 3.4).\n- School Head to institute a rotating chair system for the School‑Community Planning Team each term, documenting decisions within three days (indicator 3.2).\n- Community Liaison Officer to conduct stakeholder feedback surveys after each major event, analyze results within two weeks, and share with the leadership team.', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Shared Leadership and Data‑Driven Planning”; Result: score improved by 1.3 from 75.0% to 76.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 76.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 193, 37, '2026-10-11 18:43:51', 0),
(94, 1, '2006-2007', 28, 'Strengthen governance transparency and stakeholder feedback', '**Governance and Accountability**\nEnsure transparent processes and systematic stakeholder input.\n- Governance Committee Chair to maintain the online procurement transparency portal with weekly updates and quarterly audit reports.\n- Strategic Planning Officer to conduct an annual stakeholder satisfaction survey, compiling results and presenting recommendations by 31 July (indicator 4.6).\n- School Secretary to keep a searchable archive of all SGC meeting minutes, uploading them within two days of each meeting (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Engagement”; Result: score improved by 12.5 from 70.8% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 194, 37, '2026-10-11 18:43:51', 0),
(95, 1, '2006-2007', 29, 'Advance professional growth and staff recognition', '**Human Resource and Team Development**\nPromote consistent appraisal practices and boost morale through recognition.\n- HR Officer to finalize individualized Professional Growth Plans for all staff, reviewed semi‑annually and updated by 15 June (indicator 5.2).\n- Department Heads to launch a monthly peer‑recognition board highlighting exemplary practices, with entries submitted within five days.\n- Principal to sustain the mentorship program pairing experienced teachers with newcomers, meeting monthly and reporting progress to the HR office (indicator 5.5).', 'Last cycle: “Boost Staff Performance Management and Recognition”; Result: score improved by 7.9 from 72.1% to 80.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 195, 37, '2026-10-11 18:43:51', 0),
(96, 1, '2006-2007', 30, 'Enhance financial oversight and facility maintenance', '**Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization**\nTighten expense monitoring and ensure timely infrastructure upkeep.\n- Finance Officer to operate the electronic expense approval system, logging all MOOE requests and approving them within three business days (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to conduct monthly facility condition surveys and update the maintenance schedule, submitting a summary report by the 10th of each month (indicator 6.1).\n- Principal to lead a Cost‑Saving Task Force of teachers and staff, meeting bi‑monthly to identify savings opportunities and report recommendations within five days.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize Financial Management and Facility Oversight”; Result: score improved by 15.0 from 70.0% to 85.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 196, 37, '2026-10-11 18:43:51', 0),
(97, 1, '2006-2007', 25, 'Enhance curriculum alignment and instructional support', '**Curriculum and Teaching**\nScore rose modestly but no plan was in place, so a structured approach is needed.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to develop a competency‑based curriculum map aligned with DepEd K‑12 standards and share it school‑wide by 15 May.\n- Grade Level Leaders to schedule peer‑observation cycles where teachers observe each other twice per term and submit structured feedback within five days.\n- School Head to convene a quarterly data‑review meeting using student assessment results to adjust instructional strategies, documenting action plans within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Practices”; Result: score improved by 2.2 from 74.7% to 76.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 76.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:46:43', 0),
(98, 1, '2006-2007', 26, 'Strengthen inclusive and safe learning environment', '**Learning Environment**\nScore improved and a plan was in place, so we build on successful actions.\n- Safety Officer to continue the anti‑bullying campaign with monthly assemblies and weekly incident reviews (indicator 2.1).\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to maintain quarterly safeguarding training and add monthly reporting to ensure zero child abuse incidents (indicator 2.7, 2.2).\n- Guidance Counselor to launch an outreach program for disadvantaged, out‑of‑school and adult learners, meeting bi‑monthly and tracking participation (indicator 2.5).', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Safe and Inclusive Learning Environment”; Result: score improved by 4.2 from 71.3% to 75.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 75.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:46:43', 0),
(99, 1, '2006-2007', 27, 'Boost leadership collaboration and service innovation', '**Leadership**\nScore modestly improved; continue leadership development while fostering innovative services.\n- Assistant Principal to keep the leadership development roadmap with quarterly milestones, reviewed by the principal each quarter.\n- School Head to sustain the rotating chair system for the School‑Community Planning Team, changing chair each term and documenting decisions within three days (indicator 3.2).\n- Community Liaison Officer to pilot a Service Innovation Lab that generates two new frontline service ideas per term, with proposals reviewed by leadership within two weeks (indicator 3.4).', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Shared Leadership and Data‑Driven Planning”; Result: score improved by 1.3 from 75.0% to 76.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 76.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:46:43', 0),
(100, 1, '2006-2007', 28, 'Enhance transparency and stakeholder engagement', '**Governance and Accountability**\nSignificant gain shows effective measures; reinforce transparency and feedback loops.\n- Governance Committee Chair to keep the online procurement transparency portal updated weekly and add quarterly audit summaries (indicator 4.2).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to continue the annual stakeholder satisfaction survey and introduce a mid‑year pulse check, presenting recommendations by 31 July (indicator 4.6).\n- School Secretary to upload searchable meeting minutes within one business day of each SGC meeting and ensure they are indexed for easy retrieval (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Engagement”; Result: score improved by 12.5 from 70.8% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:46:43', 0),
(101, 1, '2006-2007', 29, 'Strengthen staff development and recognition', '**Human Resource and Team Development**\nScore improved; continue growth plans and expand recognition.\n- HR Officer to update individualized Professional Growth Plans for all staff annually, with a mid‑year review by 15 June (indicator 5.2).\n- Department Heads to maintain a monthly peer‑recognition board highlighting exemplary practices, with entries submitted within five days.\n- Principal to sustain the mentorship program pairing experienced teachers with newcomers, meeting monthly and reporting progress to the HR office (indicator 5.5).', 'Last cycle: “Boost Staff Performance Management and Recognition”; Result: score improved by 7.9 from 72.1% to 80.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:46:43', 0),
(102, 1, '2006-2007', 30, 'Optimize financial processes and facility upkeep', '**Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization**\nScore strong; keep momentum with tighter controls.\n- Finance Officer to maintain the electronic expense approval system, ensuring 100% of MOOE requests are logged and approved within three business days (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to continue monthly facility condition surveys and add a quarterly preventive maintenance schedule, submitting a summary report by the 10th of each month (indicator 6.1).\n- Principal to lead the Cost‑Saving Task Force meetings bi‑monthly, requiring each unit to submit at least one cost‑saving proposal per cycle and report recommendations within five days.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize Financial Management and Facility Oversight”; Result: score improved by 15.0 from 70.0% to 85.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 18:46:43', 0),
(103, 1, '2007-2008', 25, 'Strengthen Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Collaboration', '**Curriculum and Teaching**\nThe recent gain shows the curriculum is on the right track, yet the priority remains low and the decline risk is high, so we should deepen alignment with K‑12 standards. Implement the following actions:\n- Curriculum Coordinator to finalize a competency‑based curriculum map aligned to DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024 and circulate it to all grade level teams by 15 May.\n- Grade Level Leaders to schedule peer‑observation cycles twice each term, with teachers submitting structured feedback within five days.\n- School Head to convene a quarterly data‑review meeting using assessment results to adjust instructional strategies, documenting action plans within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum alignment and instructional support”; Result: score improved by 4.0 from 76.9% to 80.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 19:43:50', 0),
(104, 1, '2007-2008', 26, 'Bolster Child‑Protection and Safe Learning Spaces', '**Learning Environment**\nAlthough scores rose, the outlook flags a high decline risk, so reinforcing safety structures is essential. Take these steps:\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to maintain monthly anti‑bullying assemblies and conduct weekly incident reviews (indicator 2.7).\n- Guidance Counselor to expand outreach to disadvantaged learners with bi‑monthly sessions and track participation.\n- Facilities Officer to perform monthly safety inspections of classrooms and report findings to the School Head within three days.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen inclusive and safe learning environment”; Result: score improved by 7.0 from 75.5% to 82.5%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 197, 37, '2026-10-11 19:43:50', 0),
(105, 1, '2007-2008', 27, 'Advance School‑Community Planning and Innovative Services', '**Leadership**\nWith a modest increase but a high decline risk, strengthening the school‑community planning team (indicator 3.2) will sustain progress. Implement:\n- Assistant Principal to keep the leadership development roadmap with quarterly milestones, reviewed by the Principal each quarter.\n- School‑Community Planning Team Chair to rotate the chair each term and record decisions within three days (indicator 3.2).\n- Community Liaison Officer to pilot a Service Innovation Lab generating two new frontline service ideas per term, with proposals reviewed within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Boost leadership collaboration and service innovation”; Result: score improved by 7.5 from 76.3% to 83.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 198, 37, '2026-10-11 19:43:50', 0),
(106, 1, '2007-2008', 28, 'Enhance Transparency and Stakeholder Feedback Loops', '**Governance and Accountability**\nStability in score signals a need to pre‑empt potential decline; focusing on transparent processes and timely feedback is key. Actions:\n- Governance Committee Chair to publish a monthly procurement summary on the school website and add a quarterly audit brief (indicator 4.2).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to launch a mid‑year stakeholder pulse survey, compiling results and recommendations by 31 July (indicator 4.6).\n- School Secretary to upload searchable meeting minutes within one business day of each SGC meeting and ensure proper indexing (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Enhance transparency and stakeholder engagement”; Result: score was unchanged from 83.3% to 83.3%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 199, 37, '2026-10-11 19:43:50', 0),
(107, 1, '2007-2008', 29, 'Sustain Professional Growth and Recognition', '**Human Resource and Team Development**\nThe advanced score reduces immediate risk, yet maintaining momentum is important. Continue with:\n- HR Officer to update individualized Professional Growth Plans for all staff annually, with a mid‑year review by 15 June (indicator 5.2).\n- Department Heads to keep a monthly peer‑recognition board highlighting exemplary practices, with entries submitted within five days.\n- Principal to sustain the mentorship program pairing experienced teachers with newcomers, meeting monthly and reporting progress to the HR office (indicator 5.5).\n- Senior Teachers to lead quarterly Professional Learning Community sessions on instructional strategies, with attendance recorded and summary shared within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen staff development and recognition”; Result: score improved by 8.2 from 80.0% to 88.2%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 200, 37, '2026-10-11 19:43:50', 0),
(108, 1, '2007-2008', 30, 'Refine Financial Controls and Resource Optimization', '**Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization**\nWith an advanced rating, focus on fine‑tuning controls to guard against future dips. Implement:\n- Finance Officer to keep the electronic expense approval system, ensuring 100% of MOOE requests are logged and approved within three business days (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to continue monthly facility condition surveys and add a quarterly preventive maintenance schedule, submitting a summary report by the 10th of each month (indicator 6.1).\n- Principal to lead the Cost‑Saving Task Force meetings bi‑monthly, requiring each unit to submit at least one cost‑saving proposal per cycle and report recommendations within five days.\n- Procurement Officer to conduct a semi‑annual vendor performance review and publish findings to promote transparency.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize financial processes and facility upkeep”; Result: score improved by 2.9 from 85.0% to 87.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 201, 37, '2026-10-11 19:43:50', 0),
(109, 1, '2008-2009', 25, 'Deepen K‑12 curriculum alignment', 'Building on the recent score gain, further align teaching materials with the K‑12 framework.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a gap analysis of current units versus K‑12 competencies and submit findings by 30 April.\n- Grade Level Leaders to adopt competency‑based lesson‑plan templates and hold collaborative planning sessions monthly.\n- School Head to form a quarterly curriculum audit committee that reviews lesson artefacts and student performance data, reporting findings within one week of each meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Curriculum Alignment and Instructional Collaboration”; Result: score improved by 4.7 from 80.9% to 85.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 20:14:56', 0),
(110, 1, '2008-2009', 26, 'Enhance safe and inclusive learning spaces', 'To sustain the modest improvement, strengthen safety monitoring and support for vulnerable learners.\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to launch a monthly digital dashboard for bullying incidents, updated within two days of each review (indicator 2.7).\n- Facilities Officer to perform bi‑monthly classroom ergonomics checks and submit an action log to the School Head within three days.\n- Guidance Counselor to start a peer‑support program for disadvantaged learners, meeting twice a month and tracking participation in a shared register.', 'Last cycle: “Bolster Child‑Protection and Safe Learning Spaces”; Result: score improved by 1.0 from 82.5% to 83.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 202, 37, '2026-10-11 20:14:56', 0),
(111, 1, '2008-2009', 27, 'Boost frontline service innovation', 'Given the recent dip, focus on generating and piloting new service ideas for stakeholders.\n- School‑Community Planning Team Chair to convene a monthly ideation workshop with teachers, parents, and students, documenting at least two service‑improvement proposals per session (indicator 3.4).\n- Assistant Principal to assign a pilot coordinator for each approved idea, outlining implementation steps and reporting progress bi‑weekly.\n- Principal to feature successful innovations in the quarterly school newsletter, encouraging replication across grade levels.', 'Last cycle: “Advance School‑Community Planning and Innovative Services”; Result: score declined by 2.5 from 83.8% to 81.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 203, 37, '2026-10-11 20:14:56', 0),
(112, 1, '2008-2009', 28, 'Strengthen PTA engagement and governance transparency', 'Leverage the improved score by deepening parent partnership and open reporting.\n- Governance Committee Chair to formalize a PTA liaison role, meeting with the PTA chair monthly and recording minutes (indicator 4.3).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to publish a semi‑annual stakeholder pulse survey on the school website within two weeks of collection.\n- School Secretary to maintain a searchable digital archive of all SGC and PTA meeting minutes, uploaded within one business day of each meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Transparency and Stakeholder Feedback Loops”; Result: score improved by 4.2 from 83.3% to 87.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 204, 37, '2026-10-11 20:14:56', 0),
(113, 1, '2008-2009', 29, 'Revitalize staff development and mentorship', 'Address the decline by tailoring growth plans and recognizing teaching excellence.\n- HR Officer to conduct a needs‑assessment survey for all teachers by 15 May and use results to update individualized Professional Growth Plans.\n- Department Heads to schedule monthly peer‑observation cycles with structured feedback forms, completed within three days.\n- Principal to introduce a quarterly “Teaching Excellence” award, with nominations submitted by staff and winners announced at the staff assembly.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain Professional Growth and Recognition”; Result: score declined by 5.3 from 88.2% to 82.9%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 20:14:56', 0),
(114, 1, '2008-2009', 30, 'Improve MOOE utilization and facility upgrades', 'Target the sharp decline by tightening expense tracking and planning infrastructure improvements.\n- Finance Officer to monitor monthly MOOE utilization and generate a utilization report by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to develop a three‑year infrastructure improvement plan, prioritizing critical repairs, and submit quarterly progress updates by the 10th.\n- Procurement Officer to conduct a semi‑annual vendor performance review and publish findings and recommendations within two weeks of review (indicator 6.2).', 'Last cycle: “Refine Financial Controls and Resource Optimization”; Result: score declined by 9.0 from 87.9% to 78.9%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 78.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 205, 37, '2026-10-11 20:14:56', 0),
(115, 1, '2009-2010', 25, 'Refresh curriculum alignment and instructional support', '**Curriculum and Teaching**\nThe recent dip signals a need to tighten alignment with the K‑12 framework and boost teacher support.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a rapid audit of unit‑to‑competency mapping and submit a gap report by 15 May (DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024).\n- Grade Level Leaders to adopt the revised competency‑based lesson‑plan template and hold collaborative planning workshops bi‑weekly.\n- School Head to establish a monthly curriculum review meeting that monitors lesson artefacts and student performance, with minutes uploaded within two days.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen K‑12 curriculum alignment”; Result: score declined by 4.7 from 85.6% to 80.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 21:50:29', 0);
INSERT INTO `ai_suggestion_history` (`id`, `school_id`, `school_year`, `dimension_id`, `suggestion_title`, `suggestion_text`, `last_cycle_note`, `priority_label`, `decline_risk`, `data_status`, `score_at_time`, `model_version`, `is_final`, `needs_review`, `adopted_plan_id`, `generated_by`, `generated_at`, `is_sample`) VALUES
(116, 1, '2009-2010', 26, 'Strengthen safety and resilience in the learning environment', '**Learning Environment**\nGiven the decline and the emerging DRRM indicator, focus on disaster preparedness and safe spaces.\n- DRRM Committee Chair to update the school’s disaster risk reduction and management plan and conduct a drill each term, reporting compliance by 10 June (indicator 2.8).\n- Facilities Officer to perform quarterly classroom safety inspections, documenting hazards and corrective actions within three days.\n- Guidance Counselor to launch a monthly peer‑support circle for vulnerable learners, tracking attendance in a shared register.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance safe and inclusive learning spaces”; Result: score declined by 4.7 from 83.5% to 78.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 78.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 206, 37, '2026-10-11 21:50:29', 0),
(117, 1, '2009-2010', 27, 'Sustain leadership innovation and stakeholder engagement', '**Leadership**\nBuild on the recent gains by institutionalizing successful innovation practices.\n- School‑Community Planning Team Chair to embed a quarterly ideation session into the school calendar, documenting proposals and assigning pilot leads.\n- Assistant Principal to create a simple progress dashboard for each pilot, updated bi‑weekly and shared in staff meetings.\n- Principal to feature a brief “Innovation Spotlight” in the monthly newsletter, encouraging replication.', 'Last cycle: “Boost frontline service innovation”; Result: score improved by 12.5 from 81.3% to 93.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 93.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 21:50:29', 0),
(118, 1, '2009-2010', 28, 'Deepen PTA collaboration and transparent reporting', '**Governance and Accountability**\nThe drop calls for stronger parent partnership and open documentation.\n- Governance Committee Chair to schedule quarterly joint PTA‑SGC strategy workshops, producing an action plan within two weeks.\n- Governance Committee Chair to maintain the PTA liaison role, meeting the PTA chair monthly and recording minutes (indicator 4.3).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to launch a bi‑annual stakeholder pulse survey, with results posted on the school website within two weeks (indicator 4.4).', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen PTA engagement and governance transparency”; Result: score declined by 12.5 from 87.5% to 75.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 75.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 207, 37, '2026-10-11 21:50:29', 0),
(119, 1, '2009-2010', 29, 'Implement needs‑based professional development cycles', '**Human Resource and Team Development**\nAddress the dip by aligning growth plans with identified teacher needs.\n- HR Officer to administer a needs‑assessment survey for all teachers by 15 May and use results to update individualized Professional Growth Plans.\n- Department Heads to organize monthly Learning Action Cells (LAC) that target the top‑rated needs, documenting outcomes in a shared log.\n- Principal to recognize outstanding LAC contributions quarterly with a “Learning Champion” award presented at staff assembly.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize staff development and mentorship”; Result: score declined by 4.0 from 82.9% to 78.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 78.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 21:50:29', 0),
(120, 1, '2009-2010', 30, 'Refine financial monitoring and transparency', '**Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization**\nCapitalize on the recent improvement by tightening expense tracking and reporting.\n- Finance Officer to continue monthly MOOE utilization reports, submitted by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.6).\n- Facilities Manager to finalize the three‑year infrastructure improvement plan and provide quarterly progress briefs by the 10th.\n- Procurement Officer to conduct a semi‑annual vendor performance review and publish findings within two weeks (indicator 6.2).', 'Last cycle: “Improve MOOE utilization and facility upgrades”; Result: score improved by 10.0 from 78.9% to 88.9%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 208, 37, '2026-10-11 21:50:29', 0),
(121, 1, '2010-2011', 25, 'Enhance curriculum alignment and peer support', '**Curriculum Alignment** The school can fine‑tune unit‑to‑competency mapping while fostering collaborative review. - Curriculum Coordinator to lead a peer‑review of unit‑to‑competency maps, completing by 30 April. - Grade Level Leaders to schedule monthly collaborative lesson‑plan audits using the revised template, reporting findings in the curriculum review meeting. - School Head to integrate a quarterly reflection on student performance data into the curriculum review agenda, with summary posted on the school intranet within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh curriculum alignment and instructional support”; Result: score improved by 13.2 from 80.9% to 94.1%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 94.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 22:34:57', 0),
(122, 1, '2010-2011', 26, 'Deepen safety drills and learner wellbeing', '**Strengthen Safe and Supportive Learning Spaces** Recent gains can be sustained by deepening disaster readiness and wellbeing initiatives. - DRRM Committee Chair to compile quarterly drill performance reports linked to indicator 2.8 and share with staff by the 5th of the following month. - Facilities Officer to conduct a semi‑annual ergonomic audit of classroom furniture, documenting remedial actions within two weeks. - Guidance Counselor to expand peer‑support circles into a bi‑monthly resilience workshop, tracking participation in a shared log.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen safety and resilience in the learning environment”; Result: score improved by 9.0 from 78.8% to 87.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 209, 37, '2026-10-11 22:34:57', 0),
(123, 1, '2010-2011', 27, 'Empower shared leadership practices', '**Empower Shared Leadership** Maintaining high leadership scores calls for systematic mentorship and reflection. - Principal to appoint a Leadership Mentor among senior teachers to coach emerging leaders, meeting monthly. - Assistant Principal to develop a leadership competency rubric aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and use it for quarterly self‑assessments. - School‑Community Planning Team Chair to produce a brief quarterly leadership spotlight highlighting successful initiatives, disseminated via the school newsletter.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain leadership innovation and stakeholder engagement”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 93.8% to 96.3%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 96.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 22:34:57', 0),
(124, 1, '2010-2011', 28, 'Boost governance transparency and stakeholder engagement', '**Boost Governance Transparency** Building on PTA collaboration, further open documentation will reinforce accountability. - Governance Committee Chair to publish quarterly meeting minutes and action item trackers on the school website within five days of each meeting (indicator 4.3). - Strategic Planning Officer to introduce an annual public report summarizing key performance indicators, released by 30 April. - Finance Officer to integrate a simple dashboard of MOOE expenditures accessible to parents via the portal, updated monthly (indicator 6.6).', 'Last cycle: “Deepen PTA collaboration and transparent reporting”; Result: score improved by 12.5 from 75.0% to 87.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 210, 37, '2026-10-11 22:34:57', 0),
(125, 1, '2010-2011', 29, 'Advance teacher development pathways', '**Advance Teacher Development** To sustain improvement, formalize growth plans and peer coaching. - HR Officer to finalize individualized Professional Growth Plans by 31 May, linking them to identified needs from the prior survey. - Department Heads to schedule quarterly peer‑coaching cycles where teachers observe each other and provide feedback, logging outcomes. - Principal to institute a mid‑year reflective forum for teachers to share progress on growth plans, with summary circulated within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Implement needs‑based professional development cycles”; Result: score improved by 8.6 from 78.9% to 87.5%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-11 22:34:57', 0),
(126, 1, '2010-2011', 30, 'Refine financial oversight and resource allocation', '**Refine Financial Oversight** With solid reporting, deepen analysis to maximize resource impact. - Finance Officer to produce a quarterly variance analysis of MOOE vs. planned budget, highlighting corrective actions, and share with school leadership by the 10th of the following month (indicator 6.6). - Facilities Manager to integrate a bi‑annual cost‑benefit review of infrastructure projects into the three‑year plan, presenting findings to the Governance Committee. - Procurement Officer to develop a simple supplier rating matrix and update it after each semi‑annual review, publishing results on the school portal within two weeks (indicator 6.2).', 'Last cycle: “Refine financial monitoring and transparency”; Result: score improved by 3.6 from 88.9% to 92.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 92.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 211, 37, '2026-10-11 22:34:57', 0),
(127, 1, '2011-2012', 25, 'Enhance competency‑based instruction', 'Focus on aligning units with NAT proficiency and 21st‑century skill outcomes.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to audit unit‑to‑competency maps against NAT results and revise by 30 April (indicator 1.2).\n- Grade Level Leaders to hold monthly collaborative lesson‑plan reviews using the revised maps, documenting adjustments.\n- School Head to schedule quarterly data‑driven reflection meetings on NAT performance, posting summaries on the intranet within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum alignment and peer support”; Result: score declined by 14.1 from 94.1% to 80.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 00:58:38', 0),
(128, 1, '2011-2012', 26, 'Deepen disaster‑readiness and wellbeing', 'Build on safe spaces while strengthening the functional DRRM plan.\n- DRRM Committee Chair to organize semi‑annual full‑school drills linked to indicator 2.8, reporting performance within 5 days.\n- Guidance Counselor to launch bi‑monthly resilience workshops for students and staff, logging participation.\n- Facilities Officer to conduct quarterly ergonomic and safety checks of classrooms, submitting corrective‑action reports.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen safety drills and learner wellbeing”; Result: score declined by 7.5 from 87.8% to 80.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 00:58:38', 0),
(129, 1, '2011-2012', 27, 'Cultivate distributed leadership practices', 'Encourage innovation in frontline services (indicator 3.4).\n- Principal to appoint a Leadership Mentor from senior teachers to coach emerging leaders, meeting monthly and recording progress.\n- Assistant Principal to develop a leadership competency rubric aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and apply it for quarterly self‑assessments.\n- School‑Community Planning Team Chair to feature a quarterly “Leadership Spotlight” in the newsletter highlighting successful initiatives.', 'Last cycle: “Empower shared leadership practices”; Result: score declined by 19.4 from 96.3% to 76.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Medium', 'low', 'sufficient', 76.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 00:58:38', 0),
(130, 1, '2011-2012', 28, 'Strengthen governance documentation', 'Leverage the functional School Governance Council (indicator 4.2).\n- Governance Committee Chair to publish meeting minutes and action‑item tracker on the school website within three days of each meeting (indicator 4.2).\n- Strategic Planning Officer to produce an annual public performance report by 30 April, summarizing key indicators.\n- Finance Officer to update a simple MOOE dashboard monthly on the portal, ensuring transparency.', 'Last cycle: “Boost governance transparency and stakeholder engagement”; Result: score declined by 4.2 from 87.5% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 00:58:38', 0),
(131, 1, '2011-2012', 29, 'Systematize teacher growth planning', 'Address office performance commitment (indicator 5.2) and needs‑based Learning Action Cells (indicator 5.3).\n- HR Officer to finalize individualized Professional Growth Plans for all teachers by 31 May, linking to identified needs from the recent survey.\n- Department Heads to organize quarterly Learning Action Cells focused on needs‑based professional development, recording outcomes.\n- Principal to convene a mid‑year reflective forum to review progress on growth plans, circulating a summary within one week.', 'Last cycle: “Advance teacher development pathways”; Result: score declined by 12.9 from 87.5% to 74.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 74.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 00:58:38', 0),
(132, 1, '2011-2012', 30, 'Enhance resource monitoring and reporting', 'Ensure functional water, electric, and internet facilities (indicator 6.4).\n- Finance Officer to produce a quarterly variance analysis of MOOE vs. planned budget, highlighting corrective actions, and share with leadership by the 10th of the following month (indicator 6.4).\n- Facilities Manager to conduct bi‑annual audits of water, electricity, and internet services, documenting issues and remediation plans.\n- Procurement Officer to update a supplier performance log after each procurement cycle and publish on the portal within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Refine financial oversight and resource allocation”; Result: score declined by 5.4 from 92.5% to 87.1%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 00:58:38', 0),
(133, 1, '2011-2012', 25, 'Enhance Curriculum Mapping and Assessment Alignment', 'To raise the curriculum score, focus on aligning unit plans with competencies and integrating NAT performance data.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a comprehensive audit of unit‑to‑competency maps, completing by 30 April, referencing indicator 1.2.\n- Grade Level Leaders to hold monthly collaborative lesson‑plan review sessions using a revised template that links each lesson to NAT proficiency targets, with summary reports submitted to the School Head.\n- School Head to embed a quarterly reflection on NAT results into the curriculum review agenda, posting a brief analysis on the intranet within one week of each review.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum alignment and peer support”; Result: score declined by 14.1 from 94.1% to 80.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, 212, 37, '2026-10-17 00:59:31', 0),
