(150, 1, '2011-2012', 30, 'Optimize Facility Services and Resource Reliability', 'Ensuring reliable utilities (indicator 6.4) supports effective resource management.\n- Facilities Manager to conduct a semi‑annual audit of water, electricity, and internet services, reporting any issues to the Finance Officer within two weeks (indicator 6.4).\n- Finance Officer to allocate a contingency fund for immediate remediation of critical service disruptions identified in the audit, disbursing funds within ten days of approval.\n- Procurement Officer to develop a vendor performance tracker for utility providers, updating it after each service review and sharing results with school leadership quarterly.', 'Last cycle: “Refine financial oversight and resource allocation”; Result: score declined by 5.4 from 92.5% to 87.1%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:15:08', 0),
(151, 1, '2011-2012', 25, 'Strengthen Curriculum Alignment for NAT Proficiency', '**Strengthen curriculum alignment**\nFor indicator 1.2, align units to NAT proficiency targets.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to audit unit‑to‑competency maps against NAT standards and finalize revisions by 30 April.\n- Grade Level Leaders to hold monthly collaborative lesson‑plan reviews using the revised template, reporting outcomes in the curriculum review meeting.\n- School Head to post a quarterly summary of NAT performance trends on the intranet within two weeks of results release.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum alignment and peer support”; Result: score declined by 14.1 from 94.1% to 80.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:17:25', 0),
(152, 1, '2011-2012', 26, 'Deepen Safe Learning Spaces and DRRM Readiness', '**Deepen safe learning spaces**\nBuilding on the functional DRRM plan (indicator 2.8) will sustain a secure environment.\n- DRRM Committee Chair to compile quarterly drill performance reports linked to indicator 2.8 and share with staff by the 5th of the following month.\n- Guidance Counselor to launch monthly wellbeing check‑ins, documenting participation in a shared log.\n- Facilities Officer to conduct a semi‑annual ergonomic audit of classroom furniture, with remedial actions recorded within two weeks.\n- Grade Level Leaders to integrate a brief safety reflection into weekly staff meetings, summarizing any incidents or observations.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen safety drills and learner wellbeing”; Result: score declined by 7.5 from 87.8% to 80.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:17:25', 0),
(153, 1, '2011-2012', 27, 'Cultivate Shared Leadership and Service Innovation', '**Cultivate shared leadership**\nEnhancing frontline service innovation (indicator 3.4) requires coordinated mentorship.\n- Principal to establish a Leadership Development Committee with teachers and staff representatives, meeting bimonthly to set goals.\n- Senior teachers to mentor two emerging leaders each, submitting monthly reflection logs to the Assistant Principal.\n- Leadership Committee to conduct a semi‑annual review of frontline service innovations, aligning findings with indicator 3.4 and sharing results in the school assembly.\n- Assistant Principal to create a simple leadership competency rubric aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, for quarterly self‑assessment.', 'Last cycle: “Empower shared leadership practices”; Result: score declined by 19.4 from 96.3% to 76.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Medium', 'low', 'sufficient', 76.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:17:25', 0),
(154, 1, '2011-2012', 28, 'Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Access', '**Enhance governance transparency**\nA functional School Governance Council (indicator 4.2) benefits from open documentation.\n- Governance Committee Chair to publish quarterly meeting minutes and action‑item trackers on the school website within five days of each meeting (indicator 4.2).\n- PTA President to co‑host a bi‑annual open forum reviewing governance actions, with a summary posted online.\n- Strategic Planning Officer to produce an annual public report summarizing key performance indicators, released by 30 April.\n- Finance Officer to update a simple MOOE expenditure dashboard on the parent portal monthly, improving fiscal visibility.', 'Last cycle: “Boost governance transparency and stakeholder engagement”; Result: score declined by 4.2 from 87.5% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:17:25', 0),
(155, 1, '2011-2012', 29, 'Strengthen Teacher Performance Review and Collaborative Development', '**Strengthen teacher performance review**\nAddressing office performance commitment (indicator 5.2) and Learning Action Cells (indicator 5.3) will raise team capacity.\n- HR Officer to implement a bi‑annual performance appraisal system focused on office commitment, with results shared with teachers by 15 June.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to organize monthly needs‑based workshops aligned with identified gaps (indicator 5.3).\n- School Head to introduce a quarterly “Teaching Excellence” showcase where teachers present innovative practices, with peer feedback recorded.\n- Department Heads to maintain a log of peer‑coaching outcomes and review them each term.', 'Last cycle: “Advance teacher development pathways”; Result: score declined by 12.9 from 87.5% to 74.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 74.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:17:25', 0),
