(157, 1, '2012-2013', 25, 'Refresh curriculum mapping process', 'To keep curriculum delivery aligned with national standards, refresh the mapping and collaborative planning process.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to lead a comprehensive unit‑to‑competency audit against NAT proficiency targets, completing it by 30 April.\n- Grade Level Leaders to hold monthly joint lesson‑plan workshops using the updated maps, documenting adjustments in a shared drive.\n- School Head to publish a quarterly brief on curriculum alignment progress on the intranet within two weeks after each review.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Curriculum Alignment for NAT Proficiency”; Result: score declined by 0.6 from 80.0% to 79.4%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 79.40, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:31:48', 0),
(158, 1, '2012-2013', 26, 'Strengthen child‑protection protocols', 'Enhance child‑protection and overall safety by formalizing committee actions and monitoring.\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to convene bi‑monthly meetings, record attendance and action items, and file a summary report referencing indicator 2.7 by the 10th of the following month.\n- Guidance Counselor to implement a monthly zero‑incident reporting log, ensuring any reported cases are logged and reviewed in line with indicator 2.2.\n- Facilities Officer to conduct a semi‑annual safety walk‑through of classrooms and common areas, noting any hazards and corrective actions within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen Safe Learning Spaces and DRRM Readiness”; Result: score declined by 0.8 from 80.3% to 79.5%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 218, 37, '2026-10-17 01:31:48', 0),
(159, 1, '2012-2013', 27, 'Deepen leadership coaching', 'Build on strong leadership scores by expanding mentorship and reflective practice.\n- Principal to form a Leadership Mentorship Circle with senior teachers meeting bimonthly to discuss service innovations, aligning discussions with indicator 3.4.\n- Assistant Principal to introduce a quarterly self‑assessment rubric for leaders, using DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and collect completed forms within two weeks of each quarter’s end.\n- Department Heads to share one best‑practice case study from their units at each staff meeting, encouraging peer learning and documenting outcomes.', 'Last cycle: “Cultivate Shared Leadership and Service Innovation”; Result: score improved by 13.7 from 76.9% to 90.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 219, 37, '2026-10-17 01:31:48', 0),
(160, 1, '2012-2013', 28, 'Boost governance monitoring and partnerships', 'Address governance gaps by strengthening monitoring, stakeholder collaboration, and council functionality.\n- Governance Committee Chair to produce a monthly monitoring dashboard of programs and projects (indicator 4.5) and circulate it to all staff by the 5th of each month.\n- PTA President to organize a quarterly partnership forum with local NGOs and neighboring schools (indicator 4.4), summarizing agreements in a posted brief.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to ensure the council meets at least once per month, records minutes, and uploads them to the school website within five days (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Access”; Result: score declined by 12.5 from 83.3% to 70.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Medium', 'low', 'sufficient', 70.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 220, 37, '2026-10-17 01:31:48', 0),
(161, 1, '2012-2013', 29, 'Elevate teacher performance systems', 'Further raise teacher capacity by refining performance appraisal and collaborative learning structures.\n- HR Officer to launch a bi‑annual performance appraisal cycle that includes peer‑review components, with results shared with teachers by 15 June each cycle.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to schedule monthly data‑driven workshops targeting identified gaps, recording attendance and outcomes in a shared log.\n- School Head to host a quarterly “Teaching Excellence” showcase where teachers present innovative lessons, collecting peer feedback forms for professional growth records.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Teacher Performance Review and Collaborative Development”; Result: score improved by 5.4 from 74.6% to 80.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 01:31:48', 0),
(162, 1, '2012-2013', 30, 'Sustain resource reliability', 'Maintain high resource reliability by institutionalizing regular audits and transparent reporting.\n- Facilities Manager to carry out a semi‑annual audit of water, electricity, and internet services (indicator 6.4), submitting a remediation plan within two weeks of each audit.\n- Finance Officer to prepare a quarterly variance report comparing MOOE expenditures to the approved budget, highlighting corrective actions and distributing it to school leadership by the 10th of the following month.\n- Procurement Officer to update a supplier performance matrix after each procurement cycle and publish the results on the parent portal within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Optimize Resource Management and Facility Reliability”; Result: score improved by 5.8 from 87.1% to 92.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 92.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 221, 37, '2026-10-17 01:31:48', 0),
(163, 1, '2013-2014', 25, 'Boost TLE‑TV L Industry Partnerships', '**Strengthen curriculum relevance**\nEngaging local businesses can enrich the TLE‑TV L curriculum and raise student employability.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to map at least five potential industry partners and secure MOUs by 30 April (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to integrate industry‑based project outlines into lesson plans, reviewing them each month.\n- School Head to publish a quarterly brief on partnership outcomes on the intranet within two weeks after each review.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh curriculum mapping process”; Result: score declined by 1.6 from 79.4% to 77.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 77.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:09:01', 0),
(164, 1, '2013-2014', 26, 'Enhance ALS Program and Safety Monitoring', '**Elevate learning environment safety and ALS delivery**\nBuilding on the recent safety plan, integrate the ALS program to ensure comprehensive support.\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to add ALS attendance reporting to bi‑monthly meeting minutes (indicator 2.6).\n- ALS Coordinator to conduct quarterly community‑needs assessments and adjust program activities accordingly.\n- Facilities Officer to continue semi‑annual safety walk‑throughs, adding a checklist for ALS facility adequacy, with reports due within two weeks of each walk.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen child‑protection protocols”; Result: score improved by 2.8 from 79.5% to 82.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:09:01', 0),
(165, 1, '2013-2014', 27, 'Strengthen Leadership Reflective Practice', '**Deepen leadership capacity**\nFocused reflection and coaching can help sustain high leadership standards.\n- Principal to schedule monthly 1‑on‑1 coaching sessions with senior teachers, aligning discussions with indicator 3.4.\n- Assistant Principal to convene a quarterly Leadership Forum where heads present challenges and solutions, documenting outcomes.\n- Department Heads to submit brief reflective logs after each staff meeting, highlighting one actionable improvement.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen leadership coaching”; Result: score declined by 6.8 from 90.6% to 83.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:09:01', 0),
(166, 1, '2013-2014', 28, 'Sustain Governance Transparency', '**Maintain robust governance oversight**\nContinuing clear reporting keeps stakeholders informed and engaged.\n- Governance Committee Chair to circulate a concise monthly dashboard of program progress (indicator 4.5) by the 5th of each month.\n- PTA President to host a bi‑annual partnership forum with NGOs and neighboring schools (indicator 4.4), posting summaries online.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to upload meeting minutes to the school website within five days (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Boost governance monitoring and partnerships”; Result: score improved by 16.7 from 70.8% to 87.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:09:01', 0),
(167, 1, '2013-2014', 29, 'Expand Collaborative Professional Development', '**Raise teacher capacity through peer learning**\nStructured peer observation and data‑driven PLCs foster continuous growth.\n- HR Officer to launch a quarterly peer‑observation cycle, with feedback forms returned to teachers within two weeks.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to hold monthly data‑driven PLC meetings, recording attendance and action items.\n- School Head to organize an annual “Teaching Excellence” awards ceremony, collecting peer feedback for professional records.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate teacher performance systems”; Result: score improved by 6.1 from 80.0% to 86.1%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 86.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:09:01', 0),
(168, 1, '2013-2014', 30, 'Refine Financial Audit and Reporting', '**Enhance resource reliability through tighter audits**\nRegular financial scrutiny supports sustainable resource management.\n- Facilities Manager to conduct quarterly audits of water, electricity, and internet services (indicator 6.4) and submit remediation plans within two weeks.\n- Finance Officer to prepare a monthly variance report comparing MOOE expenditures to the approved budget, distributing it by the 10th of the following month.\n- Procurement Officer to update the supplier performance matrix after each procurement cycle and publish results on the parent portal within two weeks.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain resource reliability”; Result: score declined by 4.3 from 92.9% to 88.6%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:09:01', 0),
(169, 1, '2013-2014', 25, 'Boost TLE‑TVL Partnerships and Curriculum Alignment', 'Strengthen technical‑vocational curricula by linking with local industry partners and updating curriculum maps.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to map TLE‑TVL courses to at least three industry partners and finalize the partnership plan by 30 June (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to integrate industry‑led modules into weekly lesson plans and document adjustments in the shared drive starting Q3.\n- School Head to publish a quarterly brief on partnership progress on the intranet within two weeks after each review.', 'Last cycle: “Refresh curriculum mapping process”; Result: score declined by 1.6 from 79.4% to 77.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 77.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:17:51', 0),
(170, 1, '2013-2014', 26, 'Expand ALS Program and Strengthen Safety Monitoring', 'Build on recent safety gains by adding a functional ALS component and tighter monitoring.\n- ALS Coordinator to design a quarterly community outreach schedule for the ALS program and launch it by 31 March (indicator 2.6).\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to include a brief ALS safety briefing in each bi‑monthly meeting and record action items.\n- Facilities Officer to conduct quarterly safety audits of ALS classrooms, noting hazards and corrective actions within two weeks of each audit.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen child‑protection protocols”; Result: score improved by 2.8 from 79.5% to 82.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:17:51', 0);
INSERT INTO `ai_suggestion_history` (`id`, `school_id`, `school_year`, `dimension_id`, `suggestion_title`, `suggestion_text`, `last_cycle_note`, `priority_label`, `decline_risk`, `data_status`, `score_at_time`, `model_version`, `is_final`, `needs_review`, `adopted_plan_id`, `generated_by`, `generated_at`, `is_sample`) VALUES
(171, 1, '2013-2014', 27, 'Revitalize Leadership Mentorship and Reflective Practice', 'Refresh leadership development by adding structured reflection and 360‑degree feedback.\n- Principal to schedule quarterly leadership reflection retreats for senior teachers, with summaries filed by the end of each retreat.\n- Assistant Principal to launch a monthly 360‑degree feedback process using DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and collect completed forms within two weeks.\n- Department Heads to present one leadership case study at each staff meeting and record outcomes in a shared log.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen leadership coaching”; Result: score declined by 6.8 from 90.6% to 83.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:17:51', 0),
(172, 1, '2013-2014', 28, 'Institutionalize Governance Reporting and Stakeholder Engagement', 'Consolidate governance gains by automating reporting and deepening stakeholder collaboration.\n- Governance Committee Chair to develop an automated monthly dashboard of programs and projects (indicator 4.5) and circulate it by the 5th of each month.\n- PTA President to produce an annual partnership impact report summarizing NGO and school collaborations (indicator 4.4) and post it on the school website.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to create a digital archive of council minutes with searchable tags, uploading them within five days of each meeting (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Boost governance monitoring and partnerships”; Result: score improved by 16.7 from 70.8% to 87.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:17:51', 0),
(173, 1, '2013-2014', 29, 'Strengthen Professional Learning Communities and Peer Coaching', 'Enhance teacher capacity through systematic peer observation and collaborative learning.\n- HR Officer to launch a bi‑annual peer‑observation cycle with standardized feedback forms, beginning July.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host monthly data‑driven PLC meetings, recording attendance and action items in a shared log.\n- School Head to feature top collaborative teams in a quarterly staff bulletin, collecting peer feedback for professional growth records.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate teacher performance systems”; Result: score improved by 6.1 from 80.0% to 86.1%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 86.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:17:51', 0),
(174, 1, '2013-2014', 30, 'Enhance Financial Monitoring and Procurement Transparency', 'Tighten financial oversight and make procurement processes more visible.\n- Finance Officer to produce a monthly variance analysis comparing MOOE expenditures to the approved budget, highlighting corrective actions and distributing the report by the 5th of each month.\n- Procurement Officer to conduct quarterly supplier performance reviews and publish the results on the parent portal within two weeks of each review.\n- Facilities Manager to integrate semi‑annual service audit findings into the next budget revision cycle, submitting a remediation plan by 30 September (indicator 6.4).', 'Last cycle: “Sustain resource reliability”; Result: score declined by 4.3 from 92.9% to 88.6%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-17 23:17:51', 0),
(175, 1, '2014-2015', 25, 'Enhance curriculum relevance and delivery', '**Curriculum relevance and industry linkage**\nAlign TLE‑TVL courses with current industry needs to boost student employability.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a curriculum audit and map courses to at least two new industry partners, completing the plan by 30 June (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to embed industry‑led project modules into weekly lesson plans and log implementation in the shared drive by the start of Q3.\n- School Head to issue a monthly newsletter highlighting partnership outcomes and student achievements, distributed by the 5th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Boost TLE‑TVL Partnerships and Curriculum Alignment”; Result: score improved by 4.1 from 77.8% to 81.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 228, 37, '2026-10-18 00:03:07', 0),
(176, 1, '2014-2015', 26, 'Strengthen child‑protection and safety monitoring', '**Child‑Protection and safety oversight**\nBuild on the functional committee to ensure a safer learning environment.\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to conduct quarterly safety drills, document compliance, and submit findings within 10 days after each drill (indicator 2.7).\n- ALS Coordinator to finalize and launch the quarterly community outreach schedule for the ALS program by 31 March (indicator 2.6).\n- Facilities Officer to perform monthly safety audits of all classrooms, noting hazards and corrective actions within two weeks of each audit.', 'Last cycle: “Expand ALS Program and Strengthen Safety Monitoring”; Result: score declined by 3.3 from 82.3% to 79.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 79.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 229, 37, '2026-10-18 00:03:07', 0),
(177, 1, '2014-2015', 27, 'Deepen leadership reflection and peer feedback', '**Leadership reflection and feedback**\nCreate structured opportunities for leaders to reflect and receive input.\n- Principal to organize quarterly reflective retreats for senior teachers, filing summary reports within one week after each retreat.\n- Assistant Principal to launch a monthly 360‑degree feedback process using DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, collecting completed forms within two weeks of distribution.\n- Department Heads to present a leadership case study at each staff meeting and record lessons learned in a shared document by the end of the meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize Leadership Mentorship and Reflective Practice”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 83.8% to 86.3%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 86.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:03:07', 0),
(178, 1, '2014-2015', 28, 'Automate governance reporting and stakeholder engagement', '**Governance reporting automation**\nLeverage technology to keep stakeholders informed and accountable.\n- Governance Committee Chair to develop an automated monthly dashboard of programs and projects (indicator 4.5) and circulate it by the 5th of each month.\n- PTA President to compile an annual partnership impact report summarizing NGO and school collaborations (indicator 4.4) and post it on the school website by 15 April.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to maintain a digital archive of council minutes with searchable tags, uploading within five days of each meeting (indicator 4.2).', 'Last cycle: “Institutionalize Governance Reporting and Stakeholder Engagement”; Result: score declined by 4.2 from 87.5% to 83.3%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 230, 37, '2026-10-18 00:03:07', 0),
(179, 1, '2014-2015', 29, 'Expand peer observation and collaborative professional learning', '**Peer observation and PLC strengthening**\nFoster a culture of continuous improvement through shared practice.\n- HR Officer to launch a bi‑annual peer‑observation cycle with standardized feedback forms, beginning July, and submit reports within two weeks.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host monthly data‑driven PLC meetings, recording attendance and action items in a shared log by the end of each meeting.\n- School Head to feature top collaborative teams in a quarterly staff bulletin, collecting peer feedback for professional growth records, distributed by the 10th of the first month of each quarter.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Professional Learning Communities and Peer Coaching”; Result: score declined by 5.0 from 86.1% to 81.1%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:03:07', 0),
(180, 1, '2014-2015', 30, 'Enhance financial monitoring and resource alignment', '**Financial variance analysis and budgeting**\nIncrease transparency and ensure resources match school priorities.\n- Finance Officer to produce a monthly variance analysis comparing MOOE expenditures to the approved budget, highlighting corrective actions and distributing the report by the 5th of each month.\n- Procurement Officer to conduct quarterly supplier performance reviews and publish results on the parent portal within two weeks of each review.\n- Facilities Manager to integrate semi‑annual service audit findings into the next budget revision cycle, submitting a remediation plan by 30 September (indicator 6.4).', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Financial Monitoring and Procurement Transparency”; Result: score declined by 0.4 from 88.6% to 88.2%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 231, 37, '2026-10-18 00:03:07', 0),
(181, 1, '2015-2016', 25, 'Deepen industry partnership integration', 'The modest gain shows the curriculum audit is working; now embed partner projects into assessment.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to develop joint assessment rubrics with industry partners for at least two TLE‑TVL subjects, final draft by 31 July (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to schedule quarterly industry‑led workshops and record attendance in the shared drive, starting Q3.\n- School Head to feature partnership outcomes in the monthly school newsletter, distributed by the 5th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum relevance and delivery”; Result: score improved by 0.3 from 81.9% to 82.2%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 232, 37, '2026-10-18 00:25:47', 0),
(182, 1, '2015-2016', 26, 'Strengthen disaster risk reduction and safety drills', 'Building on the safety improvements, focus on the DRRM plan to close the remaining gap.\n- DRRM Committee Chair to update the school DRRM plan and conduct bi‑annual simulation drills, submitting reports within 7 days (indicator 2.8).\n- Facilities Officer to perform monthly safety inspections of evacuation routes and equipment, logging findings within two weeks.\n- School Head to communicate drill outcomes and safety tips in the weekly staff briefing, starting next month.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen child‑protection and safety monitoring”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 79.0% to 81.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 233, 37, '2026-10-18 00:25:47', 0),
(183, 1, '2015-2016', 27, 'Expand peer coaching for instructional leadership', 'With leadership scores now very high, sustain momentum through structured peer coaching.\n- Principal to initiate a monthly peer‑coaching circle among department heads, documenting key takeaways within three days after each session.\n- Assistant Principal to compile a quarterly leadership dashboard summarizing 360‑degree feedback trends, sharing with staff by the 10th of the following month (DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024).\n- Senior Teachers to mentor newly appointed teachers through bi‑monthly coaching meetings, recording progress in the staff portal.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen leadership reflection and peer feedback”; Result: score improved by 9.3 from 86.3% to 95.6%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 95.60, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:25:47', 0),
(184, 1, '2015-2016', 28, 'Activate SGC performance tracking', 'The unchanged score and emerging rating for the SGC indicate a need for clearer performance monitoring.\n- Governance Committee Chair to establish a quarterly SGC performance matrix aligned with indicator 4.2, updating it by the 15th of the month following each meeting.\n- PTA President to organize a bi‑annual stakeholder forum presenting SGC achievements and soliciting feedback, uploading minutes within five days.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to implement a searchable digital archive for all SGC documents, ensuring uploads within three days of receipt.', 'Last cycle: “Automate governance reporting and stakeholder engagement”; Result: score was unchanged from 83.3% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:25:47', 0),
(185, 1, '2015-2016', 29, 'Revitalize teacher development cycles', 'The recent dip calls for a more systematic approach to peer observation and professional learning.\n- HR Officer to design a quarterly teacher development cycle that includes self‑assessment, peer observation, and action‑plan writing, with completion reports due within two weeks after each cycle.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host monthly data‑driven PLC sessions focusing on identified instructional gaps, recording attendance and action items by end of meeting.\n- School Head to recognize exemplary teacher growth in a monthly bulletin, collecting evidence of impact by the 7th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Expand peer observation and collaborative professional learning”; Result: score declined by 0.7 from 81.1% to 80.4%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.40, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:25:47', 0),
(186, 1, '2015-2016', 30, 'Maintain financial transparency and resource alignment', 'With an advanced score, a concise sustainment focus is appropriate.\n- Finance Officer to continue monthly variance analysis reports, distributing them by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.4).\n- Procurement Officer to keep quarterly supplier performance reviews posted on the parent portal within two weeks of each review.\n- Facilities Manager to align semi‑annual service audit findings with the next budget revision, submitting remediation plan by 30 September.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance financial monitoring and resource alignment”; Result: score improved by 5.0 from 88.2% to 93.2%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 93.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 234, 37, '2026-10-18 00:25:47', 0),
(187, 1, '2016-2017', 25, 'Expand Industry‑Integrated Curriculum Design', 'To boost relevance after the recent dip, deepen collaboration with local businesses beyond workshops.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to convene a quarterly curriculum‑industry alignment meeting, producing a revised syllabus draft for two TLE‑TVL subjects by 30 September (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to pilot a joint project‑based assessment in one class per semester, documenting student outcomes and sharing results in the staff portal within two weeks of each pilot.\n- School Head to feature successful industry‑linked student projects in the monthly newsletter, with a brief impact note by the 5th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen industry partnership integration”; Result: score declined by 7.5 from 82.2% to 74.7%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Medium', 'low', 'sufficient', 74.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 235, 37, '2026-10-18 00:34:57', 0),
(188, 1, '2016-2017', 26, 'Strengthen Child‑Protection and Safety Framework', 'Given the slight decline, reinforce the child‑protection committee and safety drills.\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to update the child‑protection policy and conduct bi‑monthly staff training sessions, logging attendance within three days (indicator 2.7).\n- Facilities Officer to perform monthly checks of evacuation routes and safety equipment, submitting a concise report to the principal by the 10th of each month.\n- School Head to incorporate a brief safety tip and child‑protection reminder into the weekly staff briefing, starting next week.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen disaster risk reduction and safety drills”; Result: score declined by 1.2 from 81.5% to 80.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 236, 37, '2026-10-18 00:34:57', 0),
(189, 1, '2016-2017', 27, 'Institutionalize Leadership Peer Coaching', 'To arrest the decline, embed peer coaching into regular leadership routines.\n- Principal to schedule a monthly peer‑coaching circle for department heads, capturing key takeaways in a shared document within two days after each session.\n- Assistant Principal to prepare a quarterly leadership dashboard summarizing 360‑degree feedback trends and distribute it to all staff by the 10th of the following month (DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024).\n- Senior Teachers to mentor newly appointed teachers through bi‑monthly coaching meetings, recording progress in the staff portal within one week of each meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Expand peer coaching for instructional leadership”; Result: score declined by 5.6 from 95.6% to 90.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:34:57', 0),
(190, 1, '2016-2017', 28, 'Enhance SGC Performance Transparency', 'Improving visibility will support accountability despite stable scores.\n- Governance Committee Chair to develop a quarterly SGC performance matrix aligned with indicator 4.2, uploading it to the school intranet by the 15th of the month following each meeting.\n- PTA President to host a bi‑annual stakeholder forum presenting SGC achievements, uploading minutes to the school website within five days.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to create a searchable digital archive for all SGC documents, ensuring uploads occur within three days of receipt.', 'Last cycle: “Activate SGC performance tracking”; Result: score was unchanged from 83.3% to 83.3%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 237, 37, '2026-10-18 00:34:57', 0),
(191, 1, '2016-2017', 29, 'Systematize Teacher Development Cycle', 'A structured approach will sustain professional growth.\n- HR Officer to design a quarterly teacher development cycle that includes self‑assessment, peer observation, and action‑plan writing, with completion reports due within two weeks after each cycle.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host monthly data‑driven PLC sessions focusing on identified instructional gaps, recording attendance and action items by end of meeting.\n- School Head to recognize exemplary teacher growth in a monthly bulletin, collecting evidence of impact by the 7th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize teacher development cycles”; Result: score was unchanged from 80.4% to 80.4%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.40, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 00:34:57', 0),
(192, 1, '2016-2017', 30, 'Refine Financial Monitoring and Planning', 'Address the recent dip by tightening variance analysis and linking audits to budgeting.\n- Finance Officer to continue monthly variance analysis reports, adding a brief commentary on major deviations, and distribute them by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.4).\n- Procurement Officer to conduct quarterly supplier performance reviews and post summaries on the parent portal within two weeks of each review.\n- Facilities Manager to align semi‑annual service audit findings with the next budget revision, submitting a remediation plan by 30 September.', 'Last cycle: “Maintain financial transparency and resource alignment”; Result: score declined by 7.5 from 93.2% to 85.7%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 238, 37, '2026-10-18 00:34:57', 0),
(193, 1, '2017-2018', 25, 'Enhance curriculum relevance and instructional quality', '**Strengthen curriculum relevance**\nBuilding on recent gains, deepen instructional alignment with industry and community needs.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to launch a bi‑monthly lesson‑plan peer‑review forum, documenting revisions within five days of each session (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to integrate at least one differentiated learning activity per subject each week, reporting implementation in the monthly staff summary.\n- School Head to coordinate an annual community showcase of student projects, securing at least two external partners by 30 November.', 'Last cycle: “Expand Industry‑Integrated Curriculum Design”; Result: score improved by 5.6 from 74.7% to 80.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 80.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 239, 37, '2026-10-18 02:46:13', 0),
(194, 1, '2017-2018', 26, 'Expand learning access for disadvantaged learners', '**Broaden inclusive learning experiences**\nAddress the emerging gap in reaching out‑of‑school youth and adult learners.\n- Learning Experience Coordinator to design a monthly outreach class for disadvantaged learners, enrolling at least 15 participants per session (indicator 2.5).\n- Teachers to adapt flexible scheduling for blended learning modules, submitting weekly attendance logs to the principal.\n- School Head to allocate a modest budget for learning materials and transport subsidies, approving the allocation by 15 October.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Child‑Protection and Safety Framework”; Result: score improved by 1.7 from 80.3% to 82.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 240, 37, '2026-10-18 02:46:13', 0),
(195, 1, '2017-2018', 27, 'Deepen leadership capacity through action research', '**Elevate leadership practice**\nStrengthen strategic leadership by embedding systematic reflection.\n- Principal to initiate a quarterly action‑research cycle where department heads identify one leadership challenge, implement a pilot, and present findings at the monthly leadership meeting.\n- Assistant Principal to compile a bi‑monthly leadership insights bulletin, distributing it to all staff by the 12th of each month.\n- Senior Teachers to mentor emerging leaders through monthly coaching circles, recording progress notes within three days of each meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Institutionalize Leadership Peer Coaching”; Result: score was unchanged from 90.0% to 90.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 02:46:13', 0),
(196, 1, '2017-2018', 28, 'Strengthen stakeholder partnerships and collaboration', '**Boost collaborative partnerships**\nLeverage external networks to enrich school governance and community impact.\n- Governance Committee Chair to convene a bi‑annual partnership forum with neighboring schools and NGOs, producing a joint action plan within two weeks (indicator 4.4).\n- PTA President to coordinate a quarterly community service project involving at least two external partners, documenting outcomes by the 20th of the following month.\n- School Governance Council Secretary to maintain a shared digital repository of partnership agreements, updating it within three days of each new MOA.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance SGC Performance Transparency”; Result: score was unchanged from 83.3% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 241, 37, '2026-10-18 02:46:13', 0),
(197, 1, '2017-2018', 29, 'Advance teacher growth through peer observation', '**Enhance professional development**\nBuild on recent gains by fostering collaborative instructional improvement.\n- HR Officer to schedule monthly peer‑observation cycles, ensuring each teacher receives at least one observation per term and submits a reflective report within five days.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host a bi‑monthly data‑driven PLC focused on differentiated instruction, recording attendance and action items.\n- School Head to feature a “Teacher of the Month” spotlight in the school bulletin, highlighting observed growth and collecting evidence by the 7th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Systematize Teacher Development Cycle”; Result: score improved by 2.8 from 80.4% to 83.2%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 02:46:13', 0),
(198, 1, '2017-2018', 30, 'Increase financial transparency and strategic budgeting', '**Strengthen financial management**\nCapitalize on improved scores by deepening fiscal accountability.\n- Finance Officer to publish a concise quarterly financial summary for parents and stakeholders, posting it on the school portal within ten days after quarter‑end (indicator 6.4).\n- Procurement Officer to conduct semi‑annual supplier performance audits, sharing brief findings with the school council within two weeks of each audit.\n- Facilities Manager to align service‑audit recommendations with the next budgeting cycle, submitting a remediation plan by 30 September.', 'Last cycle: “Refine Financial Monitoring and Planning”; Result: score improved by 4.7 from 85.7% to 90.4%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.40, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 242, 37, '2026-10-18 02:46:13', 0),
(199, 1, '2018-2019', 25, 'Deepen industry‑aligned curriculum design', '**Curriculum and Teaching** Building on recent gains, further align the curriculum with local industry and community needs.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to convene a quarterly curriculum alignment workshop with local business partners, documenting revisions by the 15th of the following month (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to embed at least two project‑based learning units per subject each term, reporting implementation in the monthly staff summary.\n- School Head to approve an annual curriculum audit aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, completing the audit by 30 April.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance curriculum relevance and instructional quality”; Result: score improved by 2.2 from 80.3% to 82.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 82.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 243, 37, '2026-10-18 03:14:29', 0),
(200, 1, '2018-2019', 26, 'Expand inclusive blended learning opportunities', '**Learning Environment** Building on recent gains, broaden inclusive learning for out‑of‑school youth and adult learners.\n- Learning Experience Coordinator to design monthly outreach classes for disadvantaged learners, enrolling at least 15 participants per session and logging attendance (indicator 2.5).\n- Teachers to adopt flexible scheduling for blended modules, submitting weekly attendance logs to the principal by Friday.\n- School Head to allocate a modest budget for learning materials and transport subsidies, approving the allocation by 15 October in line with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Expand learning access for disadvantaged learners”; Result: score improved by 3.5 from 82.0% to 85.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 85.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 244, 37, '2026-10-18 03:14:29', 0),
(201, 1, '2018-2019', 27, 'Institutionalize reflective leadership cycles', '**Leadership** Strengthening an already high leadership score by embedding systematic reflection.\n- Principal to launch a quarterly action‑research cycle where each department head identifies one leadership challenge, pilots a solution, and presents findings at the monthly leadership meeting.\n- Assistant Principal to produce a bi‑monthly leadership insights bulletin, distributing it to all staff by the 12th of each month.\n- Senior Teachers to mentor emerging leaders through monthly coaching circles, recording progress notes within three days of each meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen leadership capacity through action research”; Result: score improved by 3.8 from 90.0% to 93.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 93.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 03:14:29', 0),
(202, 1, '2018-2019', 28, 'Strengthen stakeholder satisfaction and partnership monitoring', '**Governance and Accountability** Addressing the recent decline and the weak stakeholder‑satisfaction rating.\n- Governance Committee Chair to conduct a semi‑annual stakeholder satisfaction survey covering internal and external partners, compiling results and an action plan within 30 days of each survey (indicator 4.6).\n- PTA President to coordinate a quarterly partnership forum with NGOs and neighboring schools, producing a joint action plan within two weeks (indicator 4.4).\n- School Governance Council Secretary to update the digital repository of partnership agreements and survey reports within three days of any new MOA, ensuring transparency per DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen stakeholder partnerships and collaboration”; Result: score declined by 4.1 from 83.3% to 79.2%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'low', 'sufficient', 79.20, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 245, 37, '2026-10-18 03:14:29', 0),
(203, 1, '2018-2019', 29, 'Ensure timely compensation and professional growth', '**Human Resource and Team Development** Improving salary timeliness while sustaining professional development.\n- HR Officer to implement a monthly payroll verification checklist, confirming that all salaries, allowances, and additional compensation are processed by the 5th of each month (indicator 5.6).\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host a bi‑monthly data‑driven PLC focused on differentiated instruction, recording attendance and action items.\n- School Head to recognize a “Teacher of the Month” in the school bulletin, highlighting observed growth and collecting evidence by the 7th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Advance teacher growth through peer observation”; Result: score improved by 0.7 from 83.2% to 83.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 246, 37, '2026-10-18 03:14:29', 0),
(204, 1, '2018-2019', 30, 'Boost financial transparency and resource optimization', '**Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization** Responding to the slight decline by enhancing transparency and efficient budgeting.\n- Finance Officer to introduce a monthly cash‑flow dashboard accessible to the school council, updating it by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.4).\n- Procurement Officer to develop a transparent bidding log posted on the school portal, refreshed after each procurement cycle and reviewed quarterly.\n- School Head to convene a bi‑annual resource‑allocation review meeting with department heads, finalizing adjustments by 15 November in line with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Increase financial transparency and strategic budgeting”; Result: score declined by 0.4 from 90.4% to 90.0%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 247, 37, '2026-10-18 03:14:29', 0),
(205, 1, '2019-2020', 25, 'Revitalize Curriculum Alignment', 'To counter the recent dip, refocus curriculum planning on measurable outcomes and stakeholder input.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a bi‑monthly curriculum review meeting with department heads, documenting adjustments by the 10th of each month (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to integrate at least one community‑based project per subject each term, submitting implementation reports by the end of the term.\n- School Head to approve a mid‑year curriculum audit aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, completing it by 30 June.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen industry‑aligned curriculum design”; Result: score declined by 0.6 from 82.5% to 81.9%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 81.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 248, 37, '2026-10-18 03:51:51', 0),
(206, 1, '2019-2020', 26, 'Expand Inclusive Learning Programs', 'Building on the recent gains, broaden outreach and support for out‑of‑school and adult learners.\n- Learning Experience Coordinator to schedule monthly outreach classes for disadvantaged learners, targeting 20 participants per session and logging attendance (indicator 2.5).\n- Teachers to develop blended learning modules with flexible pacing, uploading them to the school portal weekly and tracking student progress.\n- School Head to allocate a quarterly budget for learning materials and transport subsidies, approving allocations by 15 October per DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Expand inclusive blended learning opportunities”; Result: score improved by 2.8 from 85.5% to 88.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 249, 37, '2026-10-18 03:51:51', 0),
(207, 1, '2019-2020', 27, 'Strengthen Leadership Reflection Practices', 'Given the recent decline, introduce structured reflection to sustain leadership effectiveness.\n- Principal to schedule semi‑annual leadership retreats with external facilitators focusing on strategic planning, with reports submitted within two weeks after each retreat.\n- Department heads to conduct monthly peer‑observation cycles, providing written feedback to each other within five days.\n- School Head to implement a quarterly 360‑degree feedback survey for all administrators, analyzing results and sharing a summary by the 20th of the following month.', 'Last cycle: “Institutionalize reflective leadership cycles”; Result: score declined by 3.8 from 93.8% to 90.0%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.00, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 03:51:51', 0),
(208, 1, '2019-2020', 28, 'Deepen Stakeholder Engagement', 'Leverage the recent improvement by strengthening systematic stakeholder collaboration.\n- Governance Committee Chair to conduct semi‑annual stakeholder satisfaction surveys (indicator 4.6), and integrate findings into the school improvement plan within 30 days.\n- PTA President to launch a quarterly partnership showcase event, inviting NGOs and neighboring schools to share best practices, with a joint action plan drafted within two weeks (indicator 4.4).\n- School Head to establish a Stakeholder Advisory Council comprising parents, community leaders, and alumni, meeting bi‑annually to review school policies and provide recommendations by 15 March and 15 September.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen stakeholder satisfaction and partnership monitoring”; Result: score improved by 8.3 from 79.2% to 87.5%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 87.50, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 250, 37, '2026-10-18 03:51:51', 0),
(209, 1, '2019-2020', 29, 'Advance Professional Development Pathways', 'Capitalize on the upward trend by formalizing continuous growth opportunities for teachers.\n- HR Officer to continue the monthly payroll verification checklist (indicator 5.6), confirming all salaries and allowances are processed by the 5th of each month.\n- HR Officer to create a monthly professional development calendar, listing internal workshops and external training opportunities, with teachers confirming attendance by the 5th of each month.\n- Learning Action Cell coordinator to host bi‑monthly data‑driven PLC sessions on differentiated instruction, recording attendance and action items.\n- School Head to institute a quarterly “Teacher Innovation Grant” program, awarding micro‑grants for classroom projects, with applications reviewed by a committee and decisions announced by the 20th of each quarter.', 'Last cycle: “Ensure timely compensation and professional growth”; Result: score improved by 5.0 from 83.9% to 88.9%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 251, 37, '2026-10-18 03:51:51', 0),
(210, 1, '2019-2020', 30, 'Enhance Financial Transparency and Planning', 'Build on the strong financial performance by deepening budget visibility and stakeholder involvement.\n- Finance Officer to maintain a monthly cash‑flow dashboard accessible to the school council, updating it by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.4).\n- Procurement Officer to publish a transparent bidding log on the school portal within three days after each procurement cycle, reviewed quarterly.\n- School Head to convene a bi‑annual resource‑allocation review meeting with department heads, finalizing adjustments by 15 November per DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.\n- School Head to introduce an annual financial literacy workshop for teachers and staff, scheduled each June, to foster understanding of budgeting processes.', 'Last cycle: “Boost financial transparency and resource optimization”; Result: score improved by 3.9 from 90.0% to 93.9%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 93.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 252, 37, '2026-10-18 03:51:51', 0),
(211, 1, '2020-2021', 25, 'Sustain curriculum excellence through data‑driven reviews', 'With the recent rise to 90.3%, it\'s important to keep momentum while guarding against potential decline.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to lead quarterly data‑analysis meetings on student performance, documenting adjustments by the 15th of the month (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to design and implement at least one interdisciplinary community‑based project per term, submitting brief reports within two weeks after term end.\n- School Head to approve an annual curriculum audit aligned with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, to be completed by 30 June and shared with teachers.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize Curriculum Alignment”; Result: score improved by 8.4 from 81.9% to 90.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 90.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 253, 37, '2026-10-18 04:03:49', 0),
(212, 1, '2020-2021', 26, 'Enhance learning environment support for diverse learners', 'Score rose modestly, but the high decline risk suggests reinforcing support structures.\n- Learning Experience Coordinator to schedule monthly outreach classes for out‑of‑school learners, targeting 20 participants per session and logging attendance (indicator 2.5).\n- Teachers to upload blended‑learning modules to the school portal weekly and record student progress in the LMS.\n- School Head to allocate a quarterly budget for learning materials and transport subsidies, approving allocations by 15 October per DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Expand Inclusive Learning Programs”; Result: score improved by 1.5 from 88.3% to 89.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 89.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 254, 37, '2026-10-18 04:03:49', 0),
(213, 1, '2020-2021', 27, 'Revitalize leadership practices with structured reflection', 'The decline to 86.9% indicates a need for stronger leadership development.\n- Principal to schedule semi‑annual leadership retreats with an external facilitator focusing on strategic planning, with post‑retreat action plans submitted within two weeks.\n- Department heads to conduct monthly peer‑observation cycles, providing written feedback within five days and summarizing trends quarterly.\n- School Head to implement a quarterly 360‑degree feedback survey for all administrators, with results presented at the monthly leadership team meeting by the 20th of the following month.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen Leadership Reflection Practices”; Result: score declined by 3.1 from 90.0% to 86.9%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 86.90, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 04:03:49', 0),
(214, 1, '2020-2021', 28, 'Strengthen stakeholder collaboration and policy review', 'The drop to 83.3% signals a need for tighter governance mechanisms.\n- Governance Committee Chair to conduct semi‑annual stakeholder satisfaction surveys (indicator 4.6) and publish a summary report on the school portal within 15 days of each survey.\n- PTA President to host a quarterly partnership showcase, inviting NGOs and neighboring schools, and develop a written memorandum of understanding for each partnership within two weeks.\n- School Head to form a Stakeholder Advisory Council that meets bi‑annually, with minutes circulated within five days and actionable recommendations submitted to the school board by 30 April and 30 October.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen Stakeholder Engagement”; Result: score declined by 4.2 from 87.5% to 83.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 255, 37, '2026-10-18 04:03:49', 0),
(215, 1, '2020-2021', 29, 'Elevate teacher development and recognition', 'The decrease to 86.4% suggests a need for enhanced professional growth mechanisms.\n- HR Officer to continue the monthly payroll verification checklist (indicator 5.6), confirming processing by the 5th of each month.\n- HR Officer to create a quarterly mentorship program pairing experienced teachers with newer staff, with mentorship plans submitted by the 15th of the first month of each quarter.\n- School Head to launch a quarterly “Teacher Innovation Grant” program, with application deadlines on the 10th of the month preceding the award announcement on the 20th.', 'Last cycle: “Advance Professional Development Pathways”; Result: score declined by 2.5 from 88.9% to 86.4%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 86.40, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 256, 37, '2026-10-18 04:03:49', 0),
(216, 1, '2020-2021', 30, 'Deepen financial transparency and staff budgeting literacy', 'The modest gain to 94.3% is encouraging, yet the high decline risk calls for sustaining transparency.\n- Finance Officer to update a monthly cash‑flow dashboard accessible to the school council by the 5th of each month (indicator 6.4).\n- Procurement Officer to publish a transparent bidding log on the school portal within three days after each procurement cycle, reviewed quarterly.\n- School Head to organize an annual financial literacy workshop for teachers and staff each June, distributing pre‑workshop materials two weeks in advance.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance Financial Transparency and Planning”; Result: score improved by 0.4 from 93.9% to 94.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 94.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1, 0, 257, 37, '2026-10-18 04:03:49', 0),
(217, 1, '2021-2022', 25, 'Curriculum Alignment & Instructional Innovation', 'The recent dip signals a need to strengthen curriculum coherence and teaching practices.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a bi‑monthly review of lesson plans against DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, submitting summary reports by the 10th of each even month (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to organize monthly peer‑lesson observations focused on interdisciplinary integration, with feedback sheets returned within three days.\n- School Head to allocate a modest fund for micro‑grants enabling teachers to pilot at least one active‑learning strategy per term, with implementation reports due within two weeks after each pilot.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain curriculum excellence through data‑driven reviews”; Result: score declined by 7.2 from 90.3% to 83.1%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:18:11', 0),
(218, 1, '2021-2022', 26, 'Learning Environment Enrichment', 'The modest gain shows positive momentum; deepening support will sustain progress.\n- Learning Experience Coordinator to maintain monthly outreach classes for out‑of‑school learners, targeting 20 participants and logging attendance in the LMS by the 5th of the following month (indicator 2.5).\n- Teachers to update blended‑learning modules weekly, adding interactive quizzes, with completion logs uploaded to the portal by Friday each week.\n- School Head to approve a quarterly budget line for classroom ergonomic upgrades (e.g., chairs, lighting), with a procurement plan submitted by 15 October each year per DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance learning environment support for diverse learners”; Result: score improved by 1.5 from 89.8% to 91.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:18:11', 0),
(219, 1, '2021-2022', 27, 'Leadership Capacity Building', 'The upward trend is encouraging, yet further development will solidify strategic direction.\n- Principal to convene quarterly strategic planning workshops with department heads, focusing on data‑driven decision‑making, with action plans documented and shared within two weeks.\n- Department heads to implement a monthly peer‑observation cycle, providing written feedback within five days.\n- School Head to implement a quarterly 360‑degree feedback survey for all administrators, with results presented at the monthly leadership team meeting by the 20th of the following month.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize leadership practices with structured reflection”; Result: score improved by 1.9 from 86.9% to 88.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:18:11', 0),
(220, 1, '2021-2022', 28, 'Governance Transparency & Stakeholder Engagement', 'The sharp rise reflects effective measures; expanding them will reinforce accountability.\n- Governance Committee Chair to continue semi‑annual stakeholder satisfaction surveys (indicator 4.6) and publish concise reports on the portal within 15 days.\n- PTA President to host quarterly partnership showcases, formalizing MOUs with partners within two weeks of each event.\n- School Head to institutionalize the Stakeholder Advisory Council meetings bi‑annually, ensuring minutes circulated within five days and actionable recommendations submitted to the board by 30 April and 30 October.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen stakeholder collaboration and policy review”; Result: score improved by 8.4 from 83.3% to 91.7%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:18:11', 0),
(221, 1, '2021-2022', 29, 'Teacher Development & Retention Boost', '**Human Resource & Team Development**\nThe recent dip indicates a need for stronger professional growth and support mechanisms.\n- HR Officer to continue the monthly payroll verification checklist (indicator 5.6), confirming processing by the 5th of each month.\n- HR Officer to redesign the mentorship program, pairing each new teacher with a mentor for a full semester, with mentorship logs submitted by the 10th of each month.\n- School Head to establish a bi‑annual Teacher Leadership Fellowship, selecting two teachers per cycle, with program outline submitted by 30 June.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate teacher development and recognition”; Result: score declined by 2.1 from 86.4% to 84.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 84.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:18:11', 0),
(222, 1, '2021-2022', 30, 'Financial Transparency & Literacy', 'The upward trend shows effective transparency; maintaining and expanding these practices will sustain confidence.\n- Finance Officer to keep updating the monthly cash‑flow dashboard (indicator 6.4) and share it with the school council by the 5th of each month.\n- Procurement Officer to continue publishing a transparent bidding log on the portal within three days after each procurement cycle, with quarterly review meetings.\n- School Head to organize an annual financial literacy workshop for teachers and staff each June, distributing pre‑workshop materials two weeks in advance.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen financial transparency and staff budgeting literacy”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 94.3% to 96.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 96.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:18:11', 0),
(223, 1, '2021-2022', 25, 'Revitalize Curriculum Alignment and Monitoring', '**Curriculum Alignment Refresh**\nWith the recent dip to 83.1%, a focused review of curriculum coherence is needed.\n- Curriculum Coordinator to conduct a monthly curriculum mapping audit against DepEd standards, submitting a brief report by the 10th of each month (indicator 1.8).\n- Grade Level Leaders to organize bi‑monthly collaborative lesson‑plan workshops, producing shared unit outlines within five days after each workshop.\n- School Head to approve a mid‑year curriculum adjustment plan, finalized by 30 April and communicated to all teachers via the school portal.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain curriculum excellence through data‑driven reviews”; Result: score declined by 7.2 from 90.3% to 83.1%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:42:03', 0),
(224, 1, '2021-2022', 26, 'Enhance Learning Environment Support Systems', '**Learning Environment Enrichment**\nThe score rose to 91.3%, but maintaining momentum requires systematic support for blended learning.\n- Learning Experience Coordinator to run monthly outreach classes for out‑of‑school learners, targeting 20 participants per session (indicator 2.5).\n- Teachers to upload at least two new blended‑learning modules to the portal each week, recording student completion rates in the LMS.\n- School Head to allocate a quarterly micro‑grant of ₱5,000 for teachers to acquire classroom resources, with applications due the 15th of the month preceding the grant cycle.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance learning environment support for diverse learners”; Result: score improved by 1.5 from 89.8% to 91.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:42:03', 0);
INSERT INTO `ai_suggestion_history` (`id`, `school_id`, `school_year`, `dimension_id`, `suggestion_title`, `suggestion_text`, `last_cycle_note`, `priority_label`, `decline_risk`, `data_status`, `score_at_time`, `model_version`, `is_final`, `needs_review`, `adopted_plan_id`, `generated_by`, `generated_at`, `is_sample`) VALUES
(225, 1, '2021-2022', 27, 'Advance Leadership Capacity and Collaboration', '**Leadership Development Cycle**\nImprovement to 88.8% shows progress; further growth can come from structured peer learning.\n- Principal to convene a quarterly leadership learning circle with an external facilitator, focusing on strategic decision‑making, with action items submitted within one week.\n- Department Heads to implement a monthly peer‑observation schedule, providing written feedback to peers within five days.\n- School Head to launch an annual 360‑degree feedback cycle for senior staff, with results presented at the first leadership team meeting of the new year.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize leadership practices with structured reflection”; Result: score improved by 1.9 from 86.9% to 88.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:42:03', 0),
(226, 1, '2021-2022', 28, 'Deepen Governance Transparency and Stakeholder Engagement', '**Governance Accountability Strengthening**\nScore now at 91.7% reflects strong governance; we can deepen stakeholder participation.\n- Governance Committee Chair to conduct semi‑annual stakeholder satisfaction surveys (indicator 4.6) and post summary reports on the portal within 15 days.\n- PTA President to coordinate a quarterly partnership showcase, securing written MOUs with each new partner within two weeks of the event.\n- School Head to establish a bi‑annual Stakeholder Advisory Council meeting, circulating minutes within five days and forwarding recommendations to the school board by 30 April and 30 October.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen stakeholder collaboration and policy review”; Result: score improved by 8.4 from 83.3% to 91.7%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:42:03', 0),
(227, 1, '2021-2022', 29, 'Elevate Teacher Development and Retention', '**Teacher Growth and Innovation**\nThe decline to 84.3% signals a need to reinforce professional development pathways.\n- HR Officer to conduct a quarterly professional development needs survey, compiling results by the 20th of the month and presenting to the school leadership team.\n- School Head to allocate a monthly “Professional Learning Stipend” of ₱2,000 for teachers attending approved external workshops, with receipts submitted within five days of attendance.\n- Department Heads to organize bi‑monthly collaborative teaching demonstrations, followed by reflective debriefs shared on the school portal within three days.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate teacher development and recognition”; Result: score declined by 2.1 from 86.4% to 84.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 84.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:42:03', 0),
(228, 1, '2021-2022', 30, 'Sustain Financial Transparency and Resource Optimization', '**Financial Transparency Continuity**\nScore reached 96.8%, indicating strong financial management; sustaining this requires regular reporting.\n- Finance Officer to prepare a quarterly financial performance brief highlighting variances, to be presented at the school council meeting within ten days after quarter end.\n- Procurement Officer to implement a bi‑annual supplier performance review, documenting compliance and sharing results with the school board by 15 May and 15 November.\n- School Head to establish a yearly “Budget Transparency Day” where staff can review the full school budget, scheduled for 1 December with preparatory materials circulated two weeks prior.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen financial transparency and staff budgeting literacy”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 94.3% to 96.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 96.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:42:03', 0),
(229, 1, '2021-2022', 25, 'D1 Curriculum and Teaching', '- Curriculum Coordinator to lead quarterly data‑driven curriculum audits, reporting findings to the School Head by the 15th of the month after each quarter.\n- Grade‑level teachers to design and implement at least two cross‑curricular project‑based learning units per semester, with lesson‑plan documentation submitted by 30 June 2022.\n- School Head to organize a biannual peer‑observation cycle focusing on instructional strategies, with feedback sessions completed within two weeks of each observation.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain curriculum excellence through data‑driven reviews”; Result: score declined by 7.2 from 90.3% to 83.1%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:54:03', 0),
(230, 1, '2021-2022', 29, 'D5 Human Resource and Team Development', '- HR Officer to create a monthly professional‑development calendar, ensuring at least one pedagogy or leadership workshop each month, finalized by 10 May 2022.\n- Department Heads to hold quarterly performance‑coaching meetings with teachers, producing individual action plans within two weeks of each meeting.\n- School Head to launch an annual teacher‑recognition program, with nominations due by 1 September 2022 and awards presented at the year‑end assembly.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate teacher development and recognition”; Result: score declined by 2.1 from 86.4% to 84.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 84.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:54:03', 0),
(231, 1, '2021-2022', 26, 'D2 Learning Environment', '- Facilities Manager to conduct biannual classroom safety and ergonomics inspections, submitting reports to the School Head by 20 March and 20 September each year.\n- ICT Coordinator to perform weekly maintenance of digital learning tools, updating a status log every Friday.\n- School Head to schedule monthly inclusive‑learning‑environment workshops for staff, the first to be held by 15 June 2022.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance learning environment support for diverse learners”; Result: score improved by 1.5 from 89.8% to 91.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:54:03', 0),
(232, 1, '2021-2022', 27, 'D3 Leadership', '- Principal to convene a quarterly leadership‑reflection forum with senior staff, circulating minutes within three days of each meeting.\n- Assistant Principal to draft a six‑month school‑improvement action plan, to be reviewed and approved by the School Head by 30 April 2022.\n- School Head to assign each department a mentor teacher for peer mentoring, with mentorship activities logged monthly and reported at the end of each term.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize leadership practices with structured reflection”; Result: score improved by 1.9 from 86.9% to 88.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:54:03', 0),
(233, 1, '2021-2022', 30, 'D6 Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization', '- Finance Officer to prepare a monthly budget‑variance report, to be reviewed by the School Head within five business days of month‑end.\n- School Head to hold a semi‑annual resource‑allocation workshop with department heads, documenting outcomes by 15 August 2022.\n- Procurement Officer to carry out a quarterly inventory audit of school supplies, submitting a summary to the Finance Officer by the 10th of the month after each quarter.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen financial transparency and staff budgeting literacy”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 94.3% to 96.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 96.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:54:03', 0),
(234, 1, '2021-2022', 28, 'D4 Governance and Accountability', '- Governance Committee Chair to organize a biannual stakeholder forum (parents and community partners) to review school policies, filing minutes within one week.\n- School Head to update the school’s accountability dashboard quarterly, ensuring data upload by the 5th of the month following each quarter.\n- Records Officer to perform a monthly compliance check against DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, reporting any gaps to the School Head within two days.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen stakeholder collaboration and policy review”; Result: score improved by 8.4 from 83.3% to 91.7%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 11:54:03', 0),
(235, 1, '2021-2022', 25, 'D1 Curriculum and Teaching', '- Curriculum Coordinator to design and integrate monthly lesson modules that embed peace education and DepEd core values, referencing indicator 1.6, to be implemented by 30 June 2023.\n- ALS Coordinator to organize quarterly certification workshops for school‑based ALS learners to achieve elementary and junior high completer status, addressing indicator 1.3, with first workshop scheduled for 15 August 2023.\n- TLE Head to partner with at least two local industries by 31 December 2023 to enrich TLE‑TVL course offerings, fulfilling indicator 1.8, and to report progress in the monthly curriculum review meeting.', 'Last cycle: “Sustain curriculum excellence through data‑driven reviews”; Result: score declined by 7.2 from 90.3% to 83.1%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 83.10, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 12:08:48', 0),
(236, 1, '2021-2022', 29, 'D5 Human Resource and Team Development', '- Human Resources Officer to coordinate an annual performance appraisal cycle that meets the very satisfactory rating criteria of indicator 5.2, with appraisal forms distributed by 1 March 2024.\n- Learning Action Cell (LAC) Facilitator to schedule needs‑based LAC sessions monthly, targeting the development areas identified in indicator 5.3, and to submit session summaries within three days after each meeting.\n- Principal to implement a bi‑monthly workload audit to verify equitable distribution of teaching assignments as required by indicator 5.7, with audit results presented at the staff meeting each second Friday.', 'Last cycle: “Elevate teacher development and recognition”; Result: score declined by 2.1 from 86.4% to 84.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 84.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 12:08:48', 0),
(237, 1, '2021-2022', 26, 'D2 Learning Environment', '- Learning Environment Officer to conduct a bi‑monthly audit of the school‑based ALS program, ensuring functionality per indicator 2.6, with audit reports submitted to the Principal by the 5th of each month.\n- Child‑Protection Committee Chair to hold quarterly awareness sessions for staff and students on child‑protection protocols, meeting the requirements of indicator 2.7, with the first session by 20 September 2023.\n- Guidance Counselor to launch a monthly dropout‑prevention tracking sheet, analyzing trends and implementing interventions to sustain the reduced drop‑out incidence noted in indicator 2.3, with initial data review by 15 October 2023.', 'Last cycle: “Enhance learning environment support for diverse learners”; Result: score improved by 1.5 from 89.8% to 91.3%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.30, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 12:08:48', 0),
(238, 1, '2021-2022', 27, 'D3 Leadership', '- School Head to convene the school‑community planning team (indicator 3.2) for a strategic planning retreat each semester, with the next retreat scheduled for 10 November 2023.\n- Student Government Adviser to facilitate a bimonthly council meeting with the Supreme Student Government (indicator 3.3) to monitor implementation of student‑led initiatives, with minutes filed by the end of each meeting.\n- Assistant Principal to review and update the school’s strategic plan (indicator 3.1) in alignment with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, completing revisions by 31 January 2024 and presenting them to the Board of Trustees.', 'Last cycle: “Revitalize leadership practices with structured reflection”; Result: score improved by 1.9 from 86.9% to 88.8%, and no improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 88.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 12:08:48', 0),
(239, 1, '2021-2022', 30, 'D6 Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization', '- Facilities Manager to perform a quarterly inspection of water, electricity, and internet services (indicator 6.4) and submit a compliance report to the Finance Officer by the 10th of the month following inspection.\n- ICT Coordinator to ensure the computer laboratory remains functional by conducting monthly equipment checks and software updates per indicator 6.5, with a status log uploaded to the school’s shared drive by the 5th of each month.\n- Finance Officer to lead a semi‑annual infrastructure audit (indicator 6.1) in line with DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024, and present findings to the School Board by 30 June 2024.', 'Last cycle: “Deepen financial transparency and staff budgeting literacy”; Result: score improved by 2.5 from 94.3% to 96.8%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 96.80, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 12:08:48', 0),
(240, 1, '2021-2022', 28, 'D4 Governance and Accountability', '- PTA President to organize a quarterly PTA‑school liaison forum to evaluate the functionality of the PTA (indicator 4.3), with the first forum on 5 October 2023.\n- Governance Committee Chair to draft a partnership memorandum of agreement with at least one external stakeholder each semester, addressing indicator 4.4, and submit to the Principal for approval within two weeks of drafting.\n- School Head to ensure the strategic plan’s implementation plan (indicator 4.1) is reviewed and reported in the monthly governance meeting, with compliance checks conducted by 15th of each month.', 'Last cycle: “Strengthen stakeholder collaboration and policy review”; Result: score improved by 8.4 from 83.3% to 91.7%, and an improvement plan was created.', 'Low', 'high', 'sufficient', 91.70, 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 0, 0, NULL, 37, '2026-10-18 12:08:48', 0),
