(533, 208, 1, 'llm', NULL, 'D6 Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization', '95.0% · −2.5 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 6.6 (avg 3.0), 6.4 (avg 3.7), 6.5 (avg 3.7)\n- School Finance Officer to conduct a quarterly audit of MOOE utilization, ensuring 75–100% usage as per indicator 6.6, and report findings to the Principal within 30 days.\n- Principal to coordinate with the Facilities Manager to verify functional water, electric, and internet services (indicator 6.4) by the end of the first quarter, and schedule maintenance if gaps are found.\n- ICT Coordinator to assess and upgrade the computer laboratory (indicator 6.5) every month, documenting equipment status and proposing budget adjustments to the Finance Officer.', '[\"6.4\",\"6.5\",\"6.6\"]', 87.60, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 13:49:29'),
(534, 208, 2, 'llm', NULL, 'D2 Learning Environment', '96.8% · +2.0 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 2.2 (avg 3.3), 2.3 (avg 3.3), 2.10 (avg 3.7)\n- School Principal to implement a zero-tolerance policy against child abuse, reinforcing indicator 2.2, by conducting staff training sessions every month.\n- Principal and Guidance Counselor to develop a dropout prevention plan addressing indicator 2.3, and monitor its implementation quarterly, reporting progress to the school board.\n- Special Education Coordinator to ensure all PWD-friendly facilities (indicator 2.10) are accessible, conducting monthly inspections and updating the facility log.', '[\"2.10\",\"2.2\",\"2.3\"]', 93.30, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 13:49:29'),
(535, 208, 3, 'llm', NULL, 'D1 Curriculum and Teaching', '89.4% · +2.8 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 1.3 (avg 3.2), 1.7 (avg 3.2), 1.6 (avg 3.3)\n- Curriculum Lead Teacher to design a certification pathway for ALS learners (indicator 1.3), rolling out a pilot in the next academic term and reviewing outcomes every month.\n- Teacher in charge of assessment to perform test item analysis (indicator 1.7) after each major assessment, sharing insights with the teaching team within 30 days.\n- Department Head to integrate peace and DepEd core values topics (indicator 1.6) into lesson plans, reviewing integration effectiveness every month.', '[\"1.3\",\"1.6\",\"1.7\"]', 100.00, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 13:49:29'),
(536, 208, 4, 'llm', NULL, 'D5 Human Resource and Team Development', '89.6% · +2.8 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 5.2 (avg 3.0), 5.4 (avg 3.2), 5.3 (avg 3.3)\n- HR Coordinator to conduct an office performance review (indicator 5.2) for all staff, completing the first cycle within 30 days and scheduling follow-up sessions quarterly.\n- HR Coordinator to organize professional development workshops (indicator 5.4) every month, tracking attendance and learning outcomes.\n- HR Coordinator to facilitate Learning Action Cells (indicator 5.3) bi-monthly, ensuring needs-based activities are documented and evaluated.', '[\"5.2\",\"5.3\",\"5.4\"]', 100.00, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 13:49:29'),
(537, 208, 5, 'llm', NULL, 'D3 Leadership', '93.1% · +3.7 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 3.2 (avg 3.0), 3.3 (avg 3.8), 3.1 (avg 4.0)\n- Principal to establish a functional school-community planning team (indicator 3.2) by the end of the first quarter, holding monthly meetings to align community goals.\n- Principal to support the Supreme Student Government (indicator 3.3) by scheduling monthly leadership workshops and monitoring student participation.\n- Principal to review and update the strategic plan (indicator 3.1) annually, with a draft review meeting every month leading up to the annual review.', '[\"3.1\",\"3.2\",\"3.3\"]', 81.70, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 13:49:29'),
(538, 208, 6, 'llm', NULL, 'D4 Governance and Accountability', '95.8% · +4.1 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 4.3 (avg 3.0), 4.1 (avg 4.0), 4.2 (avg 4.0)\n- Principal to convene the PTA (indicator 4.3) for a monthly meeting, ensuring transparent communication of school plans and budgets.\n- Principal to develop an implementation plan for the strategic plan (indicator 4.1) and conduct a quarterly review with the SGC.\n- Principal to hold monthly SGC meetings (indicator 4.2) to discuss governance issues and track action items.', '[\"4.1\",\"4.2\",\"4.3\"]', 73.30, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 13:49:29'),
(539, 209, 0, 'llm', NULL, 'AI suggestion', 'The current school year (SY 2024-2025) overall SBM score is 93.8%, compared with 93.4% in SY 2023-2024 (+0.4 percentage points). Biggest decline: D4 Governance and Accountability (−8.3 percentage points). Biggest improvement: D6 Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization (+5.0 percentage points).', '[]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00'),
(540, 209, 1, 'llm', NULL, 'D4 Governance and Accountability', '87.5% · −8.3 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 4.2 (avg 3.0), 4.3 (avg 3.0), 4.4 (avg 3.0)\n- School Head to convene a monthly meeting with the School Governance Council (SGC) to review policy implementation (4.2) and set action items, ensuring all council members submit a brief progress report within 30 days of each meeting.\n- Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) Chair to organize a quarterly workshop on partnership strategies (4.3), inviting parents and community leaders, and circulate a summary of agreed actions within 30 days after the workshop.\n- School Head to establish a bi‑monthly stakeholder collaboration forum (4.4) with local NGOs and government units, documenting partnership outcomes and sharing a brief report with the school board every month.', '[\"4.2\",\"4.3\",\"4.4\"]', 73.30, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00'),
(541, 209, 2, 'llm', NULL, 'D2 Learning Environment', '97.3% · +0.5 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 2.5 (avg 3.0), 2.10 (avg 3.3), 2.9 (avg 3.8)\n- School Head to coordinate a bi‑monthly audit of learning spaces (2.5) to identify accessibility gaps for disadvantaged learners, and assign the Facilities Manager to implement corrective actions within 30 days of each audit.\n- Special Education Coordinator to schedule a monthly training for teachers on inclusive classroom practices (2.10) and track attendance and application of strategies, reporting progress to the Head every month.\n- Mental Wellness Officer to launch a quarterly support program (2.9) for students and staff, including counseling sessions and wellness activities, and circulate a brief impact report within 30 days after each quarter.', '[\"2.10\",\"2.5\",\"2.9\"]', 93.30, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00'),
(542, 209, 3, 'llm', NULL, 'D3 Leadership', '93.8% · +0.7 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 3.2 (avg 3.0), 3.1 (avg 4.0), 3.3 (avg 4.0)\n- School Head to facilitate a monthly strategic planning session (3.1) with the leadership team, setting measurable goals and assigning owners, and circulate a concise action plan within 30 days.\n- Leadership Team Lead to convene a bi‑weekly school‑community planning meeting (3.2) to gather community input, document action items, and share a summary with stakeholders every month.\n- Student Government Chair to organize a quarterly student leadership workshop (3.3) focusing on governance skills, and submit a brief reflection report to the Head within 30 days after each workshop.', '[\"3.1\",\"3.2\",\"3.3\"]', 81.70, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00'),
(543, 209, 4, 'llm', NULL, 'D5 Human Resource and Team Development', '90.4% · +0.8 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 5.2 (avg 3.0), 5.3 (avg 3.3), 5.5 (avg 3.3)\n- HR Manager to implement a monthly performance review cycle (5.2) for all staff, ensuring feedback forms are completed and discussed within 30 days of each review.\n- Professional Development Coordinator to schedule a bi‑monthly learning action cell (5.3) for teachers, covering identified needs, and circulate a brief summary of outcomes every month.\n- School Head to establish a quarterly recognition program (5.5) celebrating milestone achievements, and publish a brief announcement to staff within 30 days after each quarter.', '[\"5.2\",\"5.3\",\"5.5\"]', 100.00, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00'),
(544, 209, 5, 'llm', NULL, 'D1 Curriculum and Teaching', '91.9% · +2.5 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 1.2 (avg 3.3), 1.3 (avg 3.3), 1.6 (avg 3.3)\n- Curriculum Lead to design a monthly lesson audit (1.2) focusing on 21st‑century skills integration, and share a concise audit report with teachers within 30 days.\n- ALS Coordinator to organize a quarterly certification preparation session (1.3) for ALS learners, and distribute a brief progress update to the Head within 30 days after each session.\n- Teacher Lead to conduct a bi‑weekly peace and values integration workshop (1.6) for staff, and compile a short reflection report to the Head every month.', '[\"1.2\",\"1.3\",\"1.6\"]', 100.00, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00'),
(545, 209, 6, 'llm', NULL, 'D6 Finance and Resource Management and Mobilization', '100.0% · +5.0 pts vs last year\nWeakest indicators: 6.1 (avg 4.0), 6.2 (avg 4.0), 6.3 (avg 4.0)\n- Finance Officer to perform a monthly inspection of infrastructure and facilities (6.1), document findings, and assign corrective actions to relevant staff within 30 days.\n- Facilities Manager to initiate a quarterly improvement plan (6.2) for identified infrastructure gaps, and report progress to the Head within 30 days after each quarter.\n- Library Coordinator to conduct a bi‑monthly library audit (6.3), assess resource availability, and circulate a brief summary of needs to the Head every month.', '[\"6.1\",\"6.2\",\"6.3\"]', 87.60, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-18 14:09:00');
